   165	The protected second pole closes Movement 6 (ch44, written at the well as day 111 breaks): "…We're going to find the other circles. Pike said nobody goes in twice. Tomorrow makes three." On this edition's calendar "tomorrow" is day 112, a road to Lowmarch's board; the next quiet ground entered is the Stair on day 114. The count is also arguable: the six have gone in at the Fallow once as a party (day 96), or twice if the first crossings at the line are counted. Sol's audit found no honest gloss. **Default until ruled: the line stays word for word, where the plan places it, unglossed.** Options: (1) keep as is (the default); (2) keep the words and move the entry to the night of day 113, the eve of the Stair, where "tomorrow" is true (Movement 6 would then close on Oryn's leaving); (3) supply replacement wording. Options 2 and 3 change published chapters.
   166	- Related, NOT an owner item: the restored protected line "I'll be three days north by the time you're back at the board" beside Oryn at Millrace (one day south of Lowmarch) on day 113 was resolved by the owner on 2026-09-04 (EXC-B7-003: "her circuit brings her round to the Stair-road stop within three days"; BOOK_MAP lists it under "do not reopen"). Movement 7's packet carries a binding note.
   167	
   168	## 52–55. Book 8 — owner items from the early plan audit (coordinator defaults, 2026-10-11)
   169	Source: `book-08-before-the-paths/state/B7-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md` §F (Sol). The audit is early: Book 7's last two movements were still open, and it is re-run when they close. Defaults below hold until the owner rules; each protected line stays word for word.
   170	- **#52 (needed before Book 8 Movement 3).** Karis's protected "right for five years or wrong for five years". Book 7 never states her hypothesis and gives it no five-year history. **Default:** the line stays verbatim as Karis's own rounding; narration does not treat five years as a fact. Options: (1) the owner confirms an older private conviction, five years old, distinct from the Book 7 hypothesis; (2) release the clause for wording without a number; (3) the default.
   171	- **#53 (needed before Book 8 Movement 4).** Protected "it took four years and a hearing to walk out". The plan itself notes the figure does not fit the academy span; #18 bars numbers for time since Kindling, and Book 7's first pole was amended on that ground. **Default:** verbatim, as Cael's rough spoken figure, never repeated as fact. Options: (1) the default; (2) release only "four years" for wording without a number, as was done for Book 7's first pole; (3) settle the series calendar so that it is true.
   172	- **#54 (needed before Book 8 Movement 9).** The plan has the young member of Teague's crew named aloud once at his death. The edition has never named Teague's crew and no name is owner-approved. **Default:** no name is minted: the cry is narrated by its effect and the name's sound is not rendered. Options: (1) the owner supplies a name before Movement 9 (it then goes in the registry and the pronunciation list); (2) the default; (3) he stays unnamed even in-world.
   173	- **#55 (needed before Book 8 Movement 9).** "Tell Lira's family I said so" (Cael's last letter to Hesk) still has no setup; this is #25, still open. **Default:** verbatim, no setup added. Options: confirm the opaque line; authorize one earlier setup beat; release or remove the clause.

