   659	### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
   660	**Calendar.** Dusk on the **hundred and twelfth day past the Line** in Oryn's window; first light on the **hundred and eleventh** for the five, at Thornwater's well. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("the cold term", "frost", "the thaw", "the snow", "the harvest", "fortnight"; "Third-day" twice, as the academy's word). Days on the page: 100, 101, 102, 103, 104, 105, 106, 107, 108, 109, 110, 111 (dawn); and, in Oryn's second window, 111 and 112. Weather: hard frost every night; ice on the trough, frozen through on the 110th; no snow. The next movement opens at Thornwater on the morning of the 111th.
   661	
   662	**Where everyone is.** The five at Thornwater, about to go out by the western gate with three boxes on Oryn's mule. Oryn two days north and west, on foot, a little short of a mill at dusk on the 112th.
