   664	**Cael.** **Nineteen** since the middle of the meal on the 102nd. **Ten confirmed fragments.** The tenth (Tide-adjacent) has been used on himself only: three days of listening, idle by the third night; one self-reading on the night of the 102nd. He has found **a place near the middle of himself that does not flow**, which all ten go round; he knows where it is, that nothing moves in it, and that none goes through; he has not named it, has not gone back to it, and has told nobody what it is. He has told Lira and then the six that there is a thing, and that it is the healer's to hear first. The three standing words are retired; the log reads *Patience is over; observation begins.* **Deployment since the Line: thirteen**; eleven leans of Wind in the yard on the 101st are logged as practice outside the number. Shadow unused; it lifts at dusk and is refused. Body whole: ribs, calf; the left forearm's feeling back to the knuckles on the 100th, a yellow mark. He has said to Oryn that it was wrong; he has not been forgiven. **He owes her:** three readings of himself on three different days, and then all of it at once; he does not know what she would have said at the door and never will; the size of the rest is hers. **The rule** is in his book in his hand, with her note under it. He has told the six that he knew at noon on the 96th. He holds a hypothesis that he has not written. Three letters still unanswered.
   665	
   666	**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. **Left arm slung and under the order until first snow; all eight marks taken at the fortnight (the 110th).** Right tibia released: it may run. **Right ankle taped, not mended; she walks on the whole sole.** She can shoot the hold's yard bow braced on a rail or across her knee, one-armed, when somebody else spans it: four of eight in a plate-sized ring from the rail at sixty paces, and one of one from the knee. She cannot span. She kept the gate-walk alone at dusk on the 110th. "Later" is discharged: she was told first. Her long knife is still blunt.
   667	
   668	**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. Hand sound, four dark lines; **Oryn's bow on his shoulder, its hook on his belt, five bolts in the sleeve.** He carried grain for the hold's bread and split a week of wood for three kinds of apple. He has spoken of his father's house twice.
   669	
   670	**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. Her voice is whole by the 110th. Points set on a lantern only (before light on the 105th; in the loft on the 110th); none on a road. In the middle box, under the heading ***the Quieting***: finding one (the name); finding two (five sigils failed *identically*; the sixth row's numeral struck, with her note and an amendment of the 110th); finding three (the floor older than her oldest dated stone; entered as a limit); finding four (the stake, once, in four sentences, "five or six"). The name is for the box only; it has not been given to Pike or to any carter. **A hypothesis, not entered and not said.** A count of kinds from the Ring, written, covered and not given out; a bowl's worth of doubtful ones that only a second site can settle. Eleven strips; the slips of bark; four chips used; the calfskin with three rings (two *guess*) and Seln's charcoal sheet. She has said the three facts to Cael and has told him that nothing about him is in the box that he has not heard to his face.
   671	
   672	**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. Unmarked. He has said that six sigils were on the road and five went out, and that he is counting it; that the west knows that something turns Paths off and does not know that something does not, "yet"; and that the record is kept. He said the birthday aloud. **Oryn has not been told that he is a source; she laid a hand on his shoulder on the 110th and said nothing. The case is on its strap, on him, shut.**
   673	
   674	**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. **She knows the mechanism** (told on the 100th, with the nine by Path). Her hands are whole. She has set: on himself first; she is the one he tells; ask, every time; three readings on three days and then all of it; nobody read on the road to find out whether he can. She has not said what she would have answered, and has not forgiven him. She read Lira's arm on the 106th and the 110th. **She has left her mule with the crew** and gone north on foot with one pannier and a spare rope, **sixteen days late out of Thornwater and seventeen at Oxhollow**, to take the next gate's beast. She has said that she goes north at first light, that Oxhollow is seventeen days late, that Thornwater is on her route, and "Don't go in without me." She has heard no theory, since nobody has offered one.
   675	
   676	**Thornwater.** The steading's woman, her husband, the bowman and the hold's boy have each had a part; none is named. The hold knows the six as the crew that came out of the Fallow, and knows nothing of what he is.
   677	
   678	**Objects and money.** Three boxes; the reserve sealed in the third, unopened. **Oryn's mule, with the crew** (one empty pannier on the saddle). Hesk's satchel: the log (the rule, the note, the second pole, the birthday line), the old volume, the notebook, the letters, the broker's posting, Pike's lines on bark including the Fallow copy. The crossbow, hook and five bolts. Board purse: **a hundred and thirty-two earned; a hundred and two in hand** (six to the hold on the 102nd). Owed: the ferryman's rope; the Fallow hundred lies in Pike's box unpaid. Hesk's parcel has not come; no boat has come in from the west since the 91st.
   679	
   680	**Pike's book and the wall.** **Eight lines**: the eighth is the protected Fallow line, entered on the 101st and sent up on bark (read aloud at the hold's board by Brom, and answered as not wrong); Pike has not said it in the crew's hearing. The wall's order after it is not known to the crew. The two HOLD slips are unresolved on the page. The broker's clerk's copy went west on the boat of the 102nd.
   681	
   682	**Vastin.** One window: a courtesy copy, read twice, not understood, filed as such, returned unannotated.
   683	
   684	**Hounds.** Unchanged: seven unaccounted for since the 96th. Nothing has come up to Thornwater's white stone since the ford (fifty-seven evenings on the 110th).
   685	
   686	**Who knows what.** The mechanism: **six.** That he knew at noon on the 96th that the fragments answered inside: the six. That he has read himself and found something: the six know that there is a thing; none knows what. The Quieting, by that name: the six. The hold, Pike, the carter, the clerk and the west know that six went in and six came out. Nobody has put a verb between a made floor, an age with no ruler, and a boy.
   687	
   688	**Open threads.** Two more readings, and a telling owed on her day. A question that she will not answer. A place that does not move. A count of kinds that wants a second floor. Two rings marked *guess* and a round that nobody can place. "One at a time, for money." A stake numbered thirty-one. A report eight days gone west. An arm slung until the snow; an ankle that nobody has mended; a bow that she can shoot and cannot span. A mule that is not theirs. Three unanswered letters and a parcel on a ferry somewhere.
   689	
   690	### Next-movement inheritance (Sol plan audit §8; also written into the next packet)
   691	Movement 7’s packet already carries the day-111 start, Oryn gone, mule with the crew, Lira two weeks into the order, and the report west (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:20`). It must additionally inherit:
   692	
   693	- **Cael:** nineteen; ten fragments; deployment thirteen; Shadow still only once; the eleven Wind leans are practice; the tenth has read only himself, once; two further self-readings on different days and the whole telling to Oryn remain owed; he may read nobody merely to test the ability; Oryn’s answer and remaining price stay withheld (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:245`; `chapter-40.md:189–211,319–385`; `chapter-44.md:167–209`).
   694	- **Bodies:** Lira’s left arm remains slung and may hold nothing until first snow, although all eight marks have taken; right tibia may run; right ankle remains taped/unmended and her left arm cannot span the bow. Brom’s hand is whole. Karis’s voice is whole but she must not lecture for a week. Cael’s calf is closed and forearm yellow-marked. Seln is unhurt (`manuscript/chapter-42.md:103–121,129–201`; `chapter-43.md:125–159`).
   695	- **Equipment and money:** 102 marks in hand; three boxes and Oryn’s mule; Seln’s shut case; Oryn’s empty pannier left on the saddle while she carries the other and the spare rope; the yard crossbow, belt hook and five bolts travel with Brom; the ring sheets, bark slips, four chips, calfskin rings and charcoal round remain in Karis’s boxes (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:55–67,379`; `chapter-41.md:3–39`; `chapter-42.md:205–277`; `chapter-43.md:171–215`; `chapter-44.md:209–245`).
   696	- **Knowledge:** all six know Cael functioned inside the Ring and know that his self-reading found something, but none except Cael knows what; Oryn knows the mechanism but not that Seln supplied Shadow; Karis’s hypothesis is neither spoken nor entered; the Quieting name and five findings are shared; nobody has put a verb between the facts (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:11–105,113–117`).
   697	- **Research state:** Karis’s kinds-count is covered and unsaid; finding four says only “five or six”; stake thirty-two remains Lira’s guess; the four wheres include two map rings marked *guess* and Seln’s unplaced childhood round (`manuscript/chapter-41.md:125–159`; `chapter-43.md:3–53`; `chapter-44.md:71–95`).
   698	- **Open accounts:** Pike has eight completed lines but the crew has not heard the eighth read at the board; the Fallow hundred remains in Pike’s box, the ferryman’s rope and two HOLD slips remain unresolved, Hesk’s parcel has not arrived, three letters are unanswered, and seven hounds remain untracked (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:221–263,383`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:173–179`).
   699	- **Oryn:** day 112 closes just short of the mill; she is sixteen late out of Thornwater and seventeen late at Oxhollow, has left the mule, and has not forgiven Cael or received the self-reading (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:223–301`). Her exact location on day 113 is Millrace under M7, subject to the protected north conflict (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:30`).
   700	
