   321	**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. He declared once at the ford, on purpose, for about three breaths, and dropped it with the hound's teeth shut on his arm; he drowned that hound with his shoulder and the current. Left forearm: closed clean on day 66, re-wrapped by his own choice, "shut, not sound". He has carried nothing since day 53. He keeps Pike's six words ("Same as anyone. What'd he do?") on a dead slip inside his shirt.
