    45	He was twelve feet from the stone when he made up his mind. He had refused Anchor, the thinnest of his ten, at these two irons the evening before, and again in the frost an hour ago. He let it look now, on purpose, with his eyes open; and since he had stopped dead to do it, he stood on a frozen road for the length of two counts while a friend with a bolt in him was being turned about by the arm.
