books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-23.md:11:"And the bearing. The kit's. He wrote *third site confirmed on bearing* and stopped. I took the bearing off his first two sites, the way he would have, and it runs along this edge. It's the same line. He found the third by walking the line from the first two, and he was right, and it's here, and we're standing on it." Her voice did not change at all, which was how they knew she meant it as method and not as fear. "Three points make a line. Four make an argument."
