books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-23.md:85:"Twenty," she said, to the cord. "Twenty cords of the line, and it bent the same every cord, the way the Ring's did. Half as much. At the Ring, twenty cords was a third of the way round it. This is twenty, and it's a sixth." She coiled the cord, once, and did not say the number, because she was Karis and a number said once was a number said, and then she said it, because it was dark and the register was the one she kept for findings she was afraid of, and a finding that was not said was not a finding. "Half the bend is twice the round. Four hundred. Near enough. Twice the radius. The same shape, at twice the size, round a thing I can't see."
