books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-23.md:119:That was the silence. Not the shape. Not the cordon. The five of them on a crest, and the one of them who could walk down that slope and over that iron and across four hundred meters of dark to a thing nobody had a word for, and come back, alone, because nothing on any of these floors had ever done anything to him — and the four who would stand at the line while he did it, with their Paths gone at a stride, and no healer's hands within four days if a thing came up under him that a floor had not taught them.
