books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-21.md:19:"Something's moved that from underneath," Seln said. "Not walked on it. Heaved it, from under the water's edge, where the marsh is soft enough to heave. It's never been out. There's no mark of anything on the top of the ridges but the weather." He did not stand up. "It lives in the water, and the water's inside the line. I don't like the stake."
