books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-21.md-46-
books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-21.md:47:"Skips are nothing to it," Seln said. He had the page. He had taken it from Karis, which nobody did, and he was writing on it in his own hand, which he had never once done in the notebook, and Karis let him. "It's blind. It reads weight on the floor. It strikes where the weight is. And it strikes what *stays*. A stone that lands and settles is hit. A stone that skips is nothing to it until it stops." He gave the page back. "That's the rule. Enter it as the rule and we'll see if it's the rule."
