books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-24.md:129:Nobody answered. Nobody said who, or why, or how old. Lira looked at the line. Brom looked at the straightedges, both of them, brass on brass. Seln looked at the map's edge where the line went off it. Cael looked at the fourth circle, twice the size of the others, with a cordon round it that nobody had drawn on the sheet because nobody had needed to. The lamp's light lay along the brass and the brass laid its shadow along the line, a hair's width, the length of the map, and the five of them looked at the shadow for four seconds, by his count, and then Karis put her hand flat on the sheet, and the evening closed.
