editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:12:> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — still-place continuity (Sol plan audit, Movement 6), binding.]** ‘The still place’ is an established private log label in locked Books 5–6, not a new phrase in Movement 8. Movement 7 must not spend the new beat: keep Cael’s finding private, unnamed aloud, and owed to Oryn. In Movement 8, the beat is that the old log label becomes a repeatedly read LOCATION and a shared spoken finding: after the second and third self-readings, Cael attaches ‘the still place’ to the located anomaly, tells Oryn while reading her with permission, and she answers the finding. Do not present the words as newly coined or new to the reader; preserve ‘Not the Quiet. Not a fragment.’ and all withheld-source limits.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:18:> - **Cael and the debt:** nineteen; ten fragments; deployment twenty-three; Shadow has now been used exactly twice and is closed for the rest of the book; Tide has read Oryn once by leave but Cael has still read himself only once. Two self-readings on different days and the full telling remain owed, Oryn's day remains hers, and neither her withheld answer nor forgiveness has been supplied (48:229–235,273–279; 51:197–225; 52:355–359).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:45:- **Day 121, the finding:** "Three points make a line. Four make an argument." The kit's bearing is the same line. The fourth circle is three days out. "I'm telling you where I'll be." / "That's a healer's sentence." / "I know whose it is."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:48:- **Home (124–129), on the page:** six days into first snow; the ribs in the cold, then quiet by the marsh's count; **Seln gives Karis the ledger** on the road and does not ask for it back; Lira's taped foot put down flat, the word *ankle* never said.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:49:- **Lowmarch (129–131):** the fifth honest catalogue, from the landing. **The season line read** (protected); the ledger turned toward him; **no number**; "too small" (protected); the room's "Eleventh." / "Aye." **Teague's term** and "Noted." The healer's single look at Brom's shoulder. **The cold-term fence** given over ("Ours.") [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]. Karis takes the back room and pays without counting (ninety-six). **The inventory** (protected; the audio rule). **The last ferry**: nine pieces sorted aloud; **Hesk's straightedge** with the note (protected); the replies west (protected). **Oryn's letter by carter** the morning after (protected): "Six, by letter." "She'll say when." / "After the thaw." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] **The map**: four circles, the bearing, both edges laid along it, **touching the three paced centres for Cael exactly as for Karis**. "The sites were on an alignment. Not random." "Someone made this pattern." Four seconds. **The closing, exact.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:51:## What must remain true / withheld
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:53:- **The fourth site is not entered and not named.** Its effect on a Path is unknown. There is no watch-post and no undated "years" on the cordon. Its silhouette stays ambiguous (Book 8 makes it an arched span on piers).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:56:- **No new maker sentence**: only "Someone made this pattern." and "a line on a map that somebody drew before there was a registry to draw one."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:58:- Lira's order stands at first snow (Oryn "will say when"). The ankle is unmended. Brom's shoulder is bound, not mended a third time. Oryn's crossbow is with Lira, with one bolt left.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:60:- Everything in `BOOK_MAP.md` §1 "Ending" is binding, as Book 8 Ch1 opens on it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:49:  - day 129: Lowmarch, first snow
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:54:- **Weather/road clock:** warm-road days give way to hard-cold days; first snow falls on the 129th. Mail-ferry schedule: inbound about the 60th and 91st; outbound on the 102nd; last run on the 130th. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:327:**Objects and money.** Three boxes over the ferry drum. The reserve unopened. Board purse: **sixty-two marks earned** (18 + ford 40 + well 4); **fifty-two in hand** (one mark on flour and bacon on day 51; one to the hold for linen and thread; coppers unitemised). Hesk's satchel holds the log (with the finding and the seal entry), the old volume, the observation notebook, Pike's two lines on bark, and Hesk's letter. Cael's coat has lost its left sleeve. The ash stick is propping an old carter's shaft under the ash.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:336:Movement 3 already carries the day-70 injury snapshot, fifty-two in hand, Teague out on two holds, the unmended ankle, and deployment count one (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:16-18,35-42`). Its author must additionally inherit:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:354:- **The herd's sense is DERIVED, not tested** (Karis: the ledge went and the declaration followed in the same breath — two causes in an accident, not one cause in a test). Derived on the 75th, used on the 78th. The animals are never given a Path. The herd's dead are "heard, not sworn"; twenty-five were counted on the 81st and the missing five are not entered as dead.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:480:- **The rubbings (flag):** one sheet to an upright, pencil rubbed over paper held flat by Lira; ten whole and the eleventh half done; numbered, with each stone's height and facing. They are in the middle box (the eleventh rolled inside Karis's coat).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:487:**Calendar.** Sunset on the **ninety-sixth day past the Line**, at the eastern lip of the Fallow Ring's floor. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("the cold term"; "frost"; "before the snow"; "fortnight"). Days on the page: 84 (dusk), 85, 86, 87, 88, 89, 90, 91, 92, 93, 94, 95, 96; and, in Teague's window, the evening of the 89th. Weather: frost every morning; dry roads; a north wind on the Fallow. The next movement opens where this one stops.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:489:**Where everyone is.** Six people at the den under the eastern lip, ten cords and half a floor inside the line: Cael, Lira, Brom (with the middle box on his back), Karis (with the eleventh sheet rolled in her coat), Seln (on one knee, the locked case on its strap across his chest) and Oryn. The lane trodden by the cord runs from the floor's western lip two hundred yards and more down to the grey stone. Oryn's mule is hobbled on the western side of the stone with her panniers, six of Thornwater's blankets, the carter's left boot and the long shape in its oiled cover still lashed on the pack. No hound has been seen. The sun is half under the hills.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:497:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. Refilled: one point on a wick on the 93rd, "three parts full"; nothing since (roads). Inside she can see every place and set none. Holds: the perimeter table (sixty-two stations, one offset); the six-row table of the trials, with the sixth ruled on his statement; **eleven finished rubbings**, ten in the box and the eleventh rolled inside her coat; the carter's map with three pencilled rings, two marked *guess*; the registry's sheet; the long cord and the short one; the brass; forty-odd chips; the leaf with her nine crossings. She has said "A circle is a made shape." once, and nobody took it up.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:505:**Objects and money.** The middle box: chips, lamp, paper, ten rubbings (the eleventh is in Karis's coat), the two maps, the brass, the short cord. Seln's case on his strap. Two boxes in Thornwater's loft, the reserve sealed in the third, unopened. The Oxhollow cart has gone home with grain. Board purse: **a hundred and thirty-two earned; a hundred and eight in hand.** Owed: one rope, sixty yards, four-strand, to the ferryman, with no price. A hundred marks lie in Pike's box against the broker's mark on the Fallow paper. Cael's coat has no sleeves.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:525:- **Maps and withheld memory:** Karis's calfskin has three circles, two marked *guess*; the registry sheet has seven dashed roads and the Fallow is the third. Seln has not yet supplied his map-memory inference; that remains M5's (`manuscript/chapter-26.md:109-149`; `MOVEMENT-004.md:54-56`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:25-26`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:549:- **The pack came home by the west (flag).** Nine came over the floor's western lip at sunset, up the party's own trodden lane, having gone out by the east at first light. Cael notes that a healer counted to ten on a wrist at that stone at noon with her Path running; "he did not know that it bore, and he put it by for whoever kept findings." It is not entered as a finding by anybody.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:573:**Calendar.** The morning of the **hundredth day past the Line**, in Thornwater's back room, in the twenty-first minute of the long reading. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("first snow", "the snow", "the harvest", "frost"). Days on the page: 96 (sunset to night), 97, 98, 99, 100. Weather: frost every night; a north wind on the Fallow; ice on Thornwater's trough.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:579:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. **Left forearm bitten through on the 96th, mended at the line; slung, and under the order until first snow** (nothing held, struck or caught). **Right ankle over a third time, taped, not mended**; she walks on the whole sole. The new tibia was run on for twenty yards and held. She knows that he chose not to act on the floor and that he had known he could; she has said "Later." and is keeping it. Her long knife is blunt.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:616:- **The telling (day 100).** Oryn named what was done to her in her own terms and set the condition — **self first, ask first, tell her** — as HERS. Cael did not argue his reasons; nothing on the page forgives him for confessing; no consent was supplied after the fact; the acquisition stands. Her answer to what she would have said at the door is withheld, from the reader too. She was told the mechanism as a RETELLING of what the five established in Book 6 (his own Arbiter woke at Kindling; the plate lit eleven seconds late; the failed-safe word; the Arbiter went dark), sources by Path and not by person except the three she has touched. **Seln is not identified to her as the source of Shadow-adjacent.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:660:**Calendar.** Dusk on the **hundred and twelfth day past the Line** in Oryn's window; first light on the **hundred and eleventh** for the five, at Thornwater's well. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("the cold term", "frost", "the thaw", "the snow", "the harvest", "fortnight"; "Third-day" twice, as the academy's word). Days on the page: 100, 101, 102, 103, 104, 105, 106, 107, 108, 109, 110, 111 (dawn); and, in Oryn's second window, 111 and 112. Weather: hard frost every night; ice on the trough, frozen through on the 110th; no snow. The next movement opens at Thornwater on the morning of the 111th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:666:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. **Left arm slung and under the order until first snow; all eight marks taken at the fortnight (the 110th).** Right tibia released: it may run. **Right ankle taped, not mended; she walks on the whole sole.** She can shoot the hold's yard bow braced on a rail or across her knee, one-armed, when somebody else spans it: four of eight in a plate-sized ring from the rail at sixty paces, and one of one from the knee. She cannot span. She kept the gate-walk alone at dusk on the 110th. "Later" is discharged: she was told first. Her long knife is still blunt.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:670:**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. Her voice is whole by the 110th. Points set on a lantern only (before light on the 105th; in the loft on the 110th); none on a road. In the middle box, under the heading ***the Quieting***: finding one (the name); finding two (five sigils failed *identically*; the sixth row's numeral struck, with her note and an amendment of the 110th); finding three (the floor older than her oldest dated stone; entered as a limit); finding four (the stake, once, in four sentences, "five or six"). The name is for the box only; it has not been given to Pike or to any carter. **A hypothesis, not entered and not said.** A count of kinds from the Ring, written, covered and not given out; a bowl's worth of doubtful ones that only a second site can settle. Eleven strips; the slips of bark; four chips used; the calfskin with three rings (two *guess*) and Seln's charcoal sheet. She has said the three facts to Cael and has told him that nothing about him is in the box that he has not heard to his face.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:693:- **Cael:** nineteen; ten fragments; deployment thirteen; Shadow still only once; the eleven Wind leans are practice; the tenth has read only himself, once; two further self-readings on different days and the whole telling to Oryn remain owed; he may read nobody merely to test the ability; Oryn’s answer and remaining price stay withheld (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:245`; `chapter-40.md:189–211,319–385`; `chapter-44.md:167–209`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:694:- **Bodies:** Lira’s left arm remains slung and may hold nothing until first snow, although all eight marks have taken; right tibia may run; right ankle remains taped/unmended and her left arm cannot span the bow. Brom’s hand is whole. Karis’s voice is whole but she must not lecture for a week. Cael’s calf is closed and forearm yellow-marked. Seln is unhurt (`manuscript/chapter-42.md:103–121,129–201`; `chapter-43.md:125–159`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:732:- **The second paper's history (flag):** written at one desk and one sitting with the first (the same pricked margin, from a wheel with a tooth missing, so that every eleventh hole stands wide; the same fault in a letter's foot); sealed inside the same wrapper, with three hundred counted in a bag and a word of direction that it was not to be posted until the first was answered; kept in the broker's strong-box, he not knowing what it was; brought up by the clerk on the morning after the Fallow line was said; said twice to the meadow, and nobody scratched; read by Teague, who hung it on the nail himself, eight days before the 112th. It carries the hook and the bar.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:734:- **The wall on the 112th:** the five are eleventh; the crew of four with the wooden foot is over them again. Pike: "The cloth can't say whose fault a thing was. It can only say what was on the cart."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:762:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. **Left arm: two marks reopened on the stair wall on the 114th, closed again that night; slung shorter, the hand at the collar-bone; under the order until first snow, and "not going to hold anything else this season".** Right ankle taped, unmended, gone once more on the stair; her tape is used up. She ran two hundred and twenty yards on the released shin. She carried the healer's bow down and held the stair with it for a day without loosing. She found sixty-two stations of an edge with her foot. Her "walk away" is entered, and she went.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:772:**Teague.** He stood for the five at Lowmarch and sat at "eleventh". He hung the second paper on the nail. He took and forfeited a four-mark slip to be near; he saw one boy, outside the edge, declare a Wind, a fire and a third thing that he cannot name; he said only that he saw a man walk out of the Quiet declaring, and asked nothing. His three walked the ruts by lantern and brought in three crossbows. He held the rim through the 115th and lent a lantern. He still has a day's posts on the forty-mark fence. His crew is unnamed; the healer of no Path has not appeared.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:787:- **Cael and the debt:** nineteen; ten fragments; deployment twenty-three; Shadow has now been used exactly twice and is closed for the rest of the book; Tide has read Oryn once by leave but Cael has still read himself only once. Two self-readings on different days and the full telling remain owed, Oryn's day remains hers, and neither her withheld answer nor forgiveness has been supplied (48:229–235,273–279; 51:197–225; 52:355–359).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:28:### Ending (Book 7 close, days 129–131 — must match the source and Book 8 Ch1)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:30:- **Where/when:** Lowmarch in first snow on the 129th day past the Line. The ferry's last run on the 130th. Oryn's letter by carter on the morning of the 131st. Book 8 Ch1 opens on the 131st.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:33:- **Lira:** left forearm bitten through at the Ring, mended at the line, reopened on the Stair and closed again. **Still slung and under Oryn's order at first snow** ("She'll say when"). Right ankle taped and **never mended in this book.** Carries Oryn's crossbow on its strap (hers from the Hall, Ch21).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:39:- **Pike's board:** **nine completed lines** under the five names (the last three are the traverse, the Ring and the Stair). The Stair's price column reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The **season line** has been read aloud. **No line number entered**: "First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small." The five names stay **eleventh** on the wall, unchanged.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:41:- **Money:** **ninety-six in hand** (a hundred and two, less six to the inn for the back room). Three hundred entered as taken and never to be paid.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:42:- **Objects:** the kit (case, pacing cord knotted at the fives, stake thirty-two with the stroke-and-bar mark and a bright point, mallet); the ledger; the 52 sheets; the map; **two brass straightedges** (Ternhall's; Hesk's, arrived on the last ferry). Both touch the three paced centres without daylight, **in Cael's hand as in anyone's** (Book 8 Ch1 owns the first hair of error). Also three boxes, Seln's case, one mule (the crew's), and Oryn's crossbow with one bolt left in it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:43:- **The Quieting, as known:** four sites on one alignment. The Fallow Ring, the Long Stair and the Drowned Hall have been entered. The fourth was paced from outside on the 123rd: **about four hundred and forty yards' radius** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2], ringed by a **cordon of iron stakes numbered thirty-four, with the stroke-and-bar mark, a pace apart**. Not entered, not named, its effect unknown, its central shape a standing grey thing nobody has a word for. "Someone made this pattern." was said once and not answered.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:45:- **Letters west on the last ferry:** to Hesk ("Nineteen, past the Line, and there's a roof…") and to Vell ("There's a second ledger on the continent…").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:86:| 31 | Lowmarch: eleventh; the room's silent verdict; Teague stands; the Stair slip at three hundred; Seln's anatomy; the council; "Inside the circle, I'm the only one who works."; Rooke quoted; Teague: "we'll come look." / "Noted." (Ch17) | 112 | KEEP |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:93:| 38 | "Three points make a line. Four make an argument."; the walk; the fork (Oryn north); five on the bearing; the fourth site, four hundred; the cordon; "Not without her…"; "We're oriented." (Ch23) | 121–123 | KEEP |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:94:| 39 | Lowmarch in first snow: the season line and no number; Teague's term; the inventory; Hesk's straightedge; letters; Oryn's letter; the map; "Someone made this pattern."; the last lines (Ch24) | 129–131 | KEEP |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:103:2. **The compressed roads and recoveries put on the page (+38,000).** The source summarizes the six days in the fin's lee and on the mountain's lip (+4k); the four days down to Oxhollow (+4k); the six days Oxhollow→Lowmarch (+4k); days 60–69 at Lowmarch and the well on the south road (+8k); the two days stone→Thornwater with Lira flat-footed (+3k); Thornwater→Lowmarch in the first cold (+2k); the three-day bearing walk (+4k); and the six days from the fourth site home in first snow (+5k). Thornwater's three stays get texture as a place that becomes home (+4k). *Why:* the arc's freedom is made of walking and of places that feed them, and the source keeps cutting it to a sentence.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:127:| 8 | 53–60 | 38,000 | 116–131 | B7 Ch21–24 | The Hall; the still place told; the wrist not read; four on a line; first snow; six by letter. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:129:**Physical challenge or learning encounter per movement:** M1 the wash recovery, the hold drilled, the Thornwater stretch walked at dusk · M2 the ford (developed fight), the well, Lira's first runs on a stiff ankle · M3 the fan haul, the bench, the stampede (terrain fight), the lip · M4 the perimeter walk and the six trials inside the line (a learning encounter for every one of the six) · M5 the Ring (central set piece), the deep reading · M6 **the deliberate quieter movement:** the bowman's one-armed shooting lessons, Cael relearning the Wind economy in Thornwater's yard under the listening, and the strata demonstration · M7 the run to the stair, the stalemate, the ascent and the rim · M8 the wyrm trials and the Hall, then the walk home into first snow.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:240:Callbacks confirmed in Book 8's closed prose: Oryn's letter and "Find me at Thornwater." / "Bring the map." (B8 Ch1, Ch24); "a tape and a season" (B8 Ch1); "Lie still when I say" (B8 Ch18, Ch24); Brom's "Twice… not three times this season" (B8 Ch6); "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it." (B8 Ch1, Ch5, Ch20); Hesk's "true to a hair" / "draw a line through it" / "Mind the shape" (B8 Ch1, Ch17, Ch18, Ch22, Ch24); "too small" (B8 Ch16, Ch17, Ch24); "Stop touching it." (B8 Ch7); "Not the Quiet." (B8 Ch7, Ch24); "He'll speak to you when you've cost him something" (B8 Ch7); Teague's after-thaw term [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] (B8 Ch1, Ch17); "Eleventh" (B8 Ch1, Ch12, Ch17); "the Bronze from Ardenmere" (B8 Ch7); ninety-six in hand (B8 Ch1); fifty-two sheets and forty-one kinds (B8 Ch9–11). Canon documents quote "Three points make a line. Four make an argument.", "Someone made this pattern.", the looms finding, "A circle is a made shape." and the stratum limit. Every other item below is a signature line or document of this book. **Keep them all exact.** Speaker attributions may be re-staged; the words may not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:294:- Ch23: *Hundred and twenty-second day, the fork. Oryn north. On her terms. I didn't ask. Five on the bearing.* — *I love this country.* — and the crest: *Four sites. One line. The last one's twice the size and the Compact fenced it. The bearing runs through it and keeps going. Karis says four points is an argument. I say it's a bearing — the kind their maps draw as nothing. Home is Lowmarch now. I just wrote that without noticing. Nineteen, ten fragments, a still place at the center of me, and a line on a map that somebody drew before there were maps. We're not done. We're oriented.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:308:- Ch11: Seln: "The road's cut." … "The grass. Where the cord went." — Oryn: "Move," … "I can't fix this here. Move." … "She keeps it." — **The order:** "A mend that deep holds nothing for a season. Nothing. That arm is not to hold. It's not to strike. It's not to catch. Not a rope, not a knife, not a fall, not a friend. Not until I say. And I'll say at first snow, near enough, if it's let alone." … "One arm. From here to the snow." — "The ankle's a tape and a season. I've told you that before." — Close: "It worked in there." / "Yours." / "Yes," Cael said. / "Later." / "Later."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:320:- Ch23: Karis: "Three points make a line. Four make an argument." — "That's a healer's sentence," Oryn said … "I know whose it is," — Brom, Lira, Oryn at the first halt: "Twice," / "Twice," / "And not three," — Oryn at the fork: "I'm three weeks late there…" … "I've been a stop on my own route for nine days. I'm going back to being the route." … "Find me at Thornwater," … "Bring the map," — Karis: "Half the bend is twice the round. Four hundred. Near enough. Twice the radius. The same shape, at twice the size, round a thing I can't see." — Seln: "That's not a survey. That's a cordon. They've been here more than once." — Lira: "Twice the size. Is it twice the *anything else*?" — Cael: "Not without her. Not without knowing what a circle twice the size does to the four of you. And not without the map finished." / "It's finished," Karis said. "It's a line." / "Then it's a line that points somewhere. We go home and find out where."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:321:- Ch24: Pike: "Teague says you need a column I don't have. I've kept this ledger thirty years. First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small." — the carters: "Eleventh," / "Aye," — Teague: "After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted," — Pike: "Fence. Forty. Teague says it's yours if you want it; he's got the cold road," / Brom: "Ours," — Lira: "She'll say when," / Brom: "After the thaw," — *The sites were on an alignment. Not random.* — Karis: "Someone made this pattern." (said once; nobody answers) — **Closing, exact:** "I have ten things that aren't a Path," Cael said, eventually, to nobody in particular, "no tier, no rank, no file I can see — and five people, one of them on a route, who've walked into the quiet three times and come out." He turned it over once and let it stand. "And a line on a map that somebody drew before there was a registry to draw one." / Lira, one-armed, feeding the fire: "Then we follow it." / Brom: "After the thaw." / Karis, writing: "Noted." / Down the fire, the man who used to file reports about him watched the snow on the ferry landing with evident professional approval and said nothing, which — from him — was home. / Nothing out here had read him. At three floors older than any registry, every Path in the party had stopped at a line and his had not; a fourth had been paced from outside and not crossed. Nobody alive — least of all him — knew why. Someone had made the pattern. That was as far as anyone could say. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] [OWNER-pending #49]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:333:| The Architect / any maker (B8 title; B11; B13–14) | Indefinite agency **only where the source has it**: "A circle is a made shape." (Ch10); "Somebody made a floor that turns Paths off." (Ch15); "Someone made this pattern." (Ch24); "a line … somebody drew before there was a registry" (Ch24). Also "Pike said a handful." | Any who, why, will, intent, reset, list of parts, "Architect," "apparatus," "un-bound" (Book 8's leaf words); any new maker sentence |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:360:- **C11 · Small counts.** Ch17 has Pike turning the ledger "which he had done once before" (it was twice: Ch2, Ch8). Ch24 has "twice in a season" (it is the fourth). Ch22 has "no captain eleven lines up" when Teague is ten up at eleventh. The retelling counts honestly. Convention: "N up" counts positions above; "N between" counts lines between.

