editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-42-- **Day 119, the Hall (≈5,000–6,000):** Brom *stops* to put Karis up the wall and the floor opens under him; he puts her up before he goes sideways. "Get *off* the floor." **The coping** as cover and trap. Karis copying the wall she kneels on, funny for exactly one exchange. **Brom's shoulder opens**; he slips on the wrong wall. **Oryn into the water, skipping**, the healer reaching a falling patient (not heroic, only nearest). **The second pass turns** toward where she is going. **Cael in, declaring:** Compression takes the strike into a standing frame at the broken edge; **Anchor laid on the floor** at the broken centre. "A thing that hunts what stays commits to the thing that stays hardest." It surfaces whole for the first time in anyone's memory. "Brom. Wall. Your weight. Now." **Four bolts into the pale**: Lira twice, braced one-armed against the coping and a knee, with Seln spanning between (the bowman's lessons pay); Seln twice. The point released; the jaws close on water; it lets go and goes down, alive. "Walls… Twelve sheets." It is left there.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-43-- **Costs at the track's end:** Oryn's hour, "Twice…" (protected); the long sit, wet to the waist; his bill (Compression in the ribs, Anchor held against biting, the read at its dearest under water). **The exchange** (protected) ending "Lie still. I want to read you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-44-- **Two days at the marsh (119–120):** two fires. Seln's blanket over Karis's shoulders. Lira keeps the bolt in the bow. Brom: "Twice." / "Twice." Oryn sleeps in front of people. **The second self-reading** (an hour; the banks a limit; **the still place**, named here for the first time; the river round a stone it has always known; four things he can count; protected log). The third before dawn: "the same." **Oryn changes the order**: "You in me." Asked and granted; surface, then a minute of the long one at her count, and while he is in, **he tells her exactly**; her finding (protected); "Write it down and stop touching it." **C3: Karis lays the cord at the Hall's perimeter** in the marsh between copies. **Teague's crew** along the track with a fifth: the older healer of no Path, "Twice?" / "Then it wants binding, not hands." The two women bind it. **Teague sits down beside him**, as Brom once did. "What are you." **The wrist a foot from his hand:** not the short reading, not the long one, not the asking. "Why did you stop reporting?" (protected exchange). "The board's going to need a new column." The log (protected). **The pencil stopping** at the far fire.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-45-- **Day 121, the finding:** "Three points make a line. Four make an argument." The kit's bearing is the same line. The fourth circle is three days out. "I'm telling you where I'll be." / "That's a healer's sentence." / "I know whose it is."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:46:- **The walk (121–122):** frost that rings; one cart of hides and a lifted hand; holds shut; the six catalogued because they will be five; the first night in a ruined hold's lee ("Twice." / "Twice." / "And not three."). **The fork:** "three weeks late there… I'm going back to being the route." He walks her fifty paces and does not ask. "Find me at Thornwater." / "Bring the map." **The four behind him, with one mule.** The log at the fork (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-47-- **Five on the bearing (122–123):** the ridge with white lines in its folds; Seln's "Nothing" every hour; **"I love this country."** at noon, with the dread in the same coat. **The fourth site from the crest at dusk:** "Larger." A valley head; a standing grey shape taller than a man, neither ring nor stair, that the dusk keeps. Lira's *gone* at about a hundred and ninety paces, not forty. Twenty cords paced along the line from outside, half the bend: four hundred. **The cordon**, iron a pace apart, numbered thirty-four with the stroke and the bar, both ways (forty counted, and more). "That's not a survey. That's a cordon…" **The council: five voices and one silence** (protected). Nobody crosses. Camp on the crest; the log (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-48-- **Home (124–129), on the page:** six days into first snow; the ribs in the cold, then quiet by the marsh's count; **Seln gives Karis the ledger** on the road and does not ask for it back; Lira's taped foot put down flat, the word *ankle* never said.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-49-- **Lowmarch (129–131):** the fifth honest catalogue, from the landing. **The season line read** (protected); the ledger turned toward him; **no number**; "too small" (protected); the room's "Eleventh." / "Aye." **Teague's term** and "Noted." The healer's single look at Brom's shoulder. **The cold-term fence** given over ("Ours.") [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]. Karis takes the back room and pays without counting (ninety-six). **The inventory** (protected; the audio rule). **The last ferry**: nine pieces sorted aloud; **Hesk's straightedge** with the note (protected); the replies west (protected). **Oryn's letter by carter** the morning after (protected): "Six, by letter." "She'll say when." / "After the thaw." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] **The map**: four circles, the bearing, both edges laid along it, **touching the three paced centres for Cael exactly as for Karis**. "The sites were on an alignment. Not random." "Someone made this pattern." Four seconds. **The closing, exact.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md-50-
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-670-**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. Her voice is whole by the 110th. Points set on a lantern only (before light on the 105th; in the loft on the 110th); none on a road. In the middle box, under the heading ***the Quieting***: finding one (the name); finding two (five sigils failed *identically*; the sixth row's numeral struck, with her note and an amendment of the 110th); finding three (the floor older than her oldest dated stone; entered as a limit); finding four (the stake, once, in four sentences, "five or six"). The name is for the box only; it has not been given to Pike or to any carter. **A hypothesis, not entered and not said.** A count of kinds from the Ring, written, covered and not given out; a bowl's worth of doubtful ones that only a second site can settle. Eleven strips; the slips of bark; four chips used; the calfskin with three rings (two *guess*) and Seln's charcoal sheet. She has said the three facts to Cael and has told him that nothing about him is in the box that he has not heard to his face.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-671-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-672-**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. Unmarked. He has said that six sigils were on the road and five went out, and that he is counting it; that the west knows that something turns Paths off and does not know that something does not, "yet"; and that the record is kept. He said the birthday aloud. **Oryn has not been told that he is a source; she laid a hand on his shoulder on the 110th and said nothing. The case is on its strap, on him, shut.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-673-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:674:**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. **She knows the mechanism** (told on the 100th, with the nine by Path). Her hands are whole. She has set: on himself first; she is the one he tells; ask, every time; three readings on three days and then all of it; nobody read on the road to find out whether he can. She has not said what she would have answered, and has not forgiven him. She read Lira's arm on the 106th and the 110th. **She has left her mule with the crew** and gone north on foot with one pannier and a spare rope, **sixteen days late out of Thornwater and seventeen at Oxhollow**, to take the next gate's beast. She has said that she goes north at first light, that Oxhollow is seventeen days late, that Thornwater is on her route, and "Don't go in without me." She has heard no theory, since nobody has offered one.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-675-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-676-**Thornwater.** The steading's woman, her husband, the bowman and the hold's boy have each had a part; none is named. The hold knows the six as the crew that came out of the Fallow, and knows nothing of what he is.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-677-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-678-**Objects and money.** Three boxes; the reserve sealed in the third, unopened. **Oryn's mule, with the crew** (one empty pannier on the saddle). Hesk's satchel: the log (the rule, the note, the second pole, the birthday line), the old volume, the notebook, the letters, the broker's posting, Pike's lines on bark including the Fallow copy. The crossbow, hook and five bolts. Board purse: **a hundred and thirty-two earned; a hundred and two in hand** (six to the hold on the 102nd). Owed: the ferryman's rope; the Fallow hundred lies in Pike's box unpaid. Hesk's parcel has not come; no boat has come in from the west since the 91st.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-695-- **Equipment and money:** 102 marks in hand; three boxes and Oryn’s mule; Seln’s shut case; Oryn’s empty pannier left on the saddle while she carries the other and the spare rope; the yard crossbow, belt hook and five bolts travel with Brom; the ring sheets, bark slips, four chips, calfskin rings and charcoal round remain in Karis’s boxes (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:55–67,379`; `chapter-41.md:3–39`; `chapter-42.md:205–277`; `chapter-43.md:171–215`; `chapter-44.md:209–245`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-696-- **Knowledge:** all six know Cael functioned inside the Ring and know that his self-reading found something, but none except Cael knows what; Oryn knows the mechanism but not that Seln supplied Shadow; Karis’s hypothesis is neither spoken nor entered; the Quieting name and five findings are shared; nobody has put a verb between the facts (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:11–105,113–117`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-697-- **Research state:** Karis’s kinds-count is covered and unsaid; finding four says only “five or six”; stake thirty-two remains Lira’s guess; the four wheres include two map rings marked *guess* and Seln’s unplaced childhood round (`manuscript/chapter-41.md:125–159`; `chapter-43.md:3–53`; `chapter-44.md:71–95`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-698-- **Open accounts:** Pike has eight completed lines but the crew has not heard the eighth read at the board; the Fallow hundred remains in Pike’s box, the ferryman’s rope and two HOLD slips remain unresolved, Hesk’s parcel has not arrived, three letters are unanswered, and seven hounds remain untracked (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:221–263,383`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:173–179`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:699:- **Oryn:** day 112 closes just short of the mill; she is sixteen late out of Thornwater and seventeen late at Oxhollow, has left the mule, and has not forgiven Cael or received the self-reading (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:223–301`). Her exact location on day 113 is Millrace under M7, subject to the protected north conflict (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:30`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-700-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-701-**Movement 6 CLOSED (2026-10-11).** Same-author repair r1: the fourteen audit fixes kept and their joins smoothed (Cael's "Then it's owed, and I've heard you say so." before Oryn's restored unit; Karis asks Oryn for a healer's count at the next edge and is not answered; Lira's "And if it's sooner than Thornwater?"); seven tracked passages restaged, ch40 scene 4 re-entered (Gault's line comes back as Brom reads Pike's bark aloud; Hesk's parcel found missing at the cleared board); ch41 now runs forward in time; the research run states its observed-versus-supposed thesis once, at the count on the night of the 103rd. Sol recheck r1: **CLOSE**, no line fixes: every brief item and all seven tracked passages resolved; the telling keeps Oryn's full agency with no retroactive consent or forgiveness; the Movement 7 joins promise neither a sixth place nor a joining. Gates 0; overlap 0 unprotected / 42 protected. 37597 words. Author-sourced sections above refreshed from the post-repair report.
