editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-72-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-73-### `[[TIER-B]]` markers: two
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-74-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-75-1. **ch54:323 — Karis, on the kerb.** The packet's `"Walls… Twelve sheets."` has a gap inside the quotation, and the map does not give the line. Before the marker: Brom's "What did we get?" After: "Nobody proposed going back for anything." No count of the Hall's sheets is printed in chapters 54–56; the twelve is first given in Karis's window (57:15) and again at the back room (60:21).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:76:2. **ch58:31 — Oryn at the fork.** The map gives `"I'm three weeks late there…"` with a trailing ellipsis. Before: "She looked along the five of them then, once, and said the thing that she had stopped the mule to say." After: the protected "I've been a stop on my own route for nine days…", whole. Nothing near it gives a figure for her lateness, or says where "there" is. (Her window gives her own sum, at 60:107: the ford with the oxen looked for her on the 104th, and the 125th is three weeks to the day.)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-77-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-78-### Stagings the coordinator may want to check
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-79-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-80-- **"Third."** is Seln's, with his hand on the breast of his coat, over the surveyor's book.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-141-2. **Oryn's "Twice. It'll hold twice…"** is given in the map with no closing punctuation. I have printed its words whole and closed it with a comma and "she said" (55:29), which stands whether or not the unit runs on. If it does run on, it wants a line fix.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-142-3. **Two markers** (ch54:323, ch58:31), as listed above.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-143-4. **The closing's form.** The map gives three of its lines with colon tags (`Lira, one-armed, feeding the fire: "Then we follow it."` / `Brom: "After the thaw."` / `Karis, writing: "Noted."`). I have printed them exactly so, as "the closing, exact" requires. If those tags are the plan's staging shorthand and not the protected wording, they want a line fix to this edition's attribution.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-144-5. **Oryn's letter is printed once**, at the end of her window (60:217), and read out in narration on the 131st (60:227). The alternative is to print it at the hearth and end her window on the pen.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:145:6. **"Three weeks."** Since the fork's first sentence is a marker, the only sum on the page is in her window: the ford with the oxen looked for her on the 104th, and she comes down out of the gap on the 125th. BOOK_MAP §1 says "at Thornwater on her route, three weeks late there"; I have not asserted that of Thornwater, where the edition's own round would make her eleven days behind.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-146-7. **The old woman's knee.** The packet says "the old woman at Thornwater"; Movement 7 mended that knee at Millrace and sent her home up the valley. I have had her walk to Thornwater on it, so that "The knee held." is a thing Oryn's hands have checked.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-147-8. **The count and the inventory.** The trial point of the 118th is counted as the twenty-fourth deployment. The protected inventory says that Anchor has been "used… twice this year, once each way". The day's log covers it ("Counted in the number. I'll not call a trial a use."). If the coordinator would rather the trial were left out of the number, as the noon tests of the 96th were, the final count is twenty-seven and three log lines change.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-148-9. **Ephram is not answered.** Two letters go west, as §1 lists. Cael notes that the third "would go by the first boat of the thaw". Book 8 may want to know that this is promised.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-149-10. **The clerk's packet** goes west on the last ferry (60:87). It can say only that the crew kept what it was sent for. Nothing in it, or in Pike's ninth line as said, tells the west that anything worked inside a line.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-161-**Where everyone is.** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln at the lower inn, sleeping at the hearth's end, with the store behind the chimney for the paper. Oryn at Thornwater, two days up a saddle that the carter does not expect to cross again before the thaw; she meant to go north by the wicket when the bench was paid (two days more from the 127th), and her letter was written on the evening of the 128th. Teague, the spear, the bow, the boy and the older healer at Lowmarch for the cold term.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-162-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-163-**Cael.** Nineteen. **Ten confirmed fragments.** **Deployment since the Line: twenty-eight** (the ford 1; the Ring 12; Oryn on the ridge 1; the Stair 9; the Hall's kerb 1; the Hall 3; Oryn at the marsh 1). Shadow used twice in all and shut. Anchor: looked three times; unbound once (the Stair); set twice (the kerb, sixty counts; the slab in the breach). Tide: Oryn twice, each time by her leave; himself three times (102, 119, 120); nobody else; never inside a line. **The still place:** his old log label, now a location under the breastbone, read three times; nothing moves in it; all ten go round it and none through; they do not pile against it; not the Quiet; not a fragment; told to Oryn at once and in order on the 120th, and to the other four in three sentences on the 121st; he has been told to write it down and stop touching it, and has not touched it since. Body: ribs quiet since the morning of the 129th; right forearm and left palm no longer remarked; calf a closed seam. Hesk's satchel: the log (the entries of the 118th, 119th, 120th, the fork, the crest, and the inventory of the 129th), the old volume, the notebook, Hesk's letter and note, Ephram's and Vell's letters, both of the broker's papers, Pike's lines on bark, and Oryn's letter on bark. **He has Hesk's brass straightedge.** He has said "Noted" to Teague three times. He has not answered Ephram.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-164-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:165:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst in this movement. **Left arm slung high, all eight marks taken (read by Oryn at the fork on the 122nd), still under the order: it holds nothing until Oryn says, and she has not said; five weeks on the 131st.** It held nothing in a fall on the ice on the 127th. **Right ankle taped, never mended**; she walks on the whole sole; Oryn left her a roll at the fork. **She carries Oryn's crossbow on its strap, spanned, with one bolt in it**; she cannot span it; she shot it twice in the Hall and hit twice. She has not asked for the ankle again.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-166-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-167-**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. **Right shoulder: bolted on the 114th and mended; opened on the Hall's wall on the 119th and mended a second time; bound on the 120th by Teague's healer and Oryn in four yards of webbing, with a drover's turn; not to be mended a third time this season; the knot not to be undone except by that woman, who looked at it on the 129th and said "It'll do."** He carries the kit on his left side. He lays six bowls and, since the letter, has left the sixth out. He took the fence: "Ours,".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-168-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/movement-008/AUTHOR-REPORT.md-169-**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. Points set on a fire and a lamp only. **Fifty-two sheets** (eleven, twenty-nine, twelve), in three heaps in the back room. **Forty-one kinds** at the two sites done properly; thirty-three of them, and none strange, on the Hall's one wall; the lone line seen there and not measured. Three perimeters of one size and the fourth site's radius by the bend: four hundred and forty yards and two strides. **The kit's field ledger, given her by Seln.** The leaf of the three places, in four copies (one to a box, one in her coat with the trials leaf). **The carter's map with four rings, the third moved and the fourth unlabelled, and a pencil line through the three paced centres and on off the hide.** The Ternhall brass. She has said "Someone made this pattern." once, aloud, and nobody answered. **Her hypothesis is unentered and unsaid.** She paid six marks without counting and keeps the purse.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-33-- **Lira:** left forearm bitten through at the Ring, mended at the line, reopened on the Stair and closed again. **Still slung and under Oryn's order at first snow** ("She'll say when"). Right ankle taped and **never mended in this book.** Carries Oryn's crossbow on its strap (hers from the Hall, Ch21).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-34-- **Brom:** right shoulder bolted on the Stair and mended, reopened in the Hall and mended a second time ("Twice… not three times this season"). Then bound by Teague's healer of no Path and carried guarded. Carries the kit and the middle box.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-35-- **Karis:** holds the field archive: **52 sheets** of copied walls (Ring 11 / Stair 29 / Hall 12); the kit's **field ledger** (given her by Seln on the road home); the carter's map with **four circles and the bearing**; the Ternhall straightedge. She named the Quieting. Her hypothesis stays unentered. She has the inn's back room for the sheets.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-36-- **Seln:** unmarked all book. The case carried, unopened, targeted, kept. Angry once (the Stair's rim: "No faces." and a broken stock).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:37:- **Oryn:** at Thornwater on her route, **three weeks late there** and the route whole. Letter: "Six, by letter." She learned the mechanism on the 100th. She has not heard any theory, because there is none.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-38-- **Who knows the mechanism:** six (Oryn added). Teague, Pike, the holds and the faceless faction do not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-39-- **Pike's board:** **nine completed lines** under the five names (the last three are the traverse, the Ring and the Stair). The Stair's price column reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The **season line** has been read aloud. **No line number entered**: "First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small." The five names stay **eleventh** on the wall, unchanged.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-40-- **Teague:** "After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted." His crew (four plus an older healer of no Path) stays at Lowmarch through the cold term. He has given the axe-head hold's long fence (forty, HOLD) to the five for the cold term. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2; restates protected Ch24 — OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-41-- **Money:** **ninety-six in hand** (a hundred and two, less six to the inn for the back room). Three hundred entered as taken and never to be paid.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-316-- Ch19: Brom: "Ridge," — Seln: "They can shoot the bowl," … "They can't shoot the stair." — Oryn: "I can see what's wrong. I can't feel it and I can't touch it. Tape it. Leave the bolt." … "the bolt's the plug" … "I came south for exactly this. Enter that." — Oryn: "Ask first," — Lira: "Later." / "Later." — Oryn at the stone: "There. Back," … "The clock started again." — "It held a stair. It's not going to hold anything else this season." — Seln: "No faces." — Teague: "You walked out of the Quiet declaring," / "Yes." … "Then you're not on the board anymore. You're something the board doesn't have a column for."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-317-- Ch20: Teague: "We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted" — Oryn: "What are they" / Karis: "Lines," — Karis: "He tried to drive it. Twice, by the head. It wouldn't go. Nothing goes into this." — Seln: "Nobody leaves a registry kit. It's signed out. You don't get another." … "I don't know what this is in, and I'm not going to say." — Karis: "Forty-one," … "every ten cords and a piece. Two hundred and twenty yards and a stride, to the stride." … "The floor was carved by somebody who knew the circle's size," … "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-318-- Ch21: Oryn: "Big. Under. Comes up. Nobody's seen it whole." — Seln: "It's blind. It reads weight on the floor. It strikes where the weight is. And it strikes what *stays*." — Karis: "It reads that as the heaviest thing on the floor," / Cael: "It reads that as the thing that *stays*," — Lira: "We're going in without Paths to look at walls with a thing under the floor." / "Yes," Karis said. / "Just checking that's the plan." — Seln: "It's blind. It reads the floor. Get *off* the floor." — "You're copying," / "I'm not getting another chance," / "No, I can see that you're not," — *A thing that hunts what stays commits to the thing that stays hardest.* — "Brom," Cael said. "Wall. Your weight. Now." — Oryn: "Twice. It'll hold twice. It will not hold three times this season, so don't ask it to" — "You went in the water." / "You went in for Brom." / "Brom's on my route." … "So are you." … "Lie still. I want to read you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-319-- Ch22: Oryn: "A still place that everything goes around. I've never felt that in anyone." / "Is it wrong?" / "I don't know what right would look like in you. Nobody does. That's not a comfort; it's a finding." … "Write it down and stop touching it. Things you keep touching don't heal." — Teague's healer: "Twice?" … "Then it wants binding, not hands," — Teague: "What are you." / Cael: "Why did you stop reporting?" / "Because the board pays the same whether I do or don't," … "and the registry doesn't, and I'd sooner be worth what I did than what they wrote." … "That's not an answer to mine." / "No." / "You didn't answer." / "I don't have one. Neither does the board. You said so." / "I did." … "The board's going to need a new column."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:320:- Ch23: Karis: "Three points make a line. Four make an argument." — "That's a healer's sentence," Oryn said … "I know whose it is," — Brom, Lira, Oryn at the first halt: "Twice," / "Twice," / "And not three," — Oryn at the fork: "I'm three weeks late there…" … "I've been a stop on my own route for nine days. I'm going back to being the route." … "Find me at Thornwater," … "Bring the map," — Karis: "Half the bend is twice the round. Four hundred. Near enough. Twice the radius. The same shape, at twice the size, round a thing I can't see." — Seln: "That's not a survey. That's a cordon. They've been here more than once." — Lira: "Twice the size. Is it twice the *anything else*?" — Cael: "Not without her. Not without knowing what a circle twice the size does to the four of you. And not without the map finished." / "It's finished," Karis said. "It's a line." / "Then it's a line that points somewhere. We go home and find out where."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-321-- Ch24: Pike: "Teague says you need a column I don't have. I've kept this ledger thirty years. First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small." — the carters: "Eleventh," / "Aye," — Teague: "After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted," — Pike: "Fence. Forty. Teague says it's yours if you want it; he's got the cold road," / Brom: "Ours," — Lira: "She'll say when," / Brom: "After the thaw," — *The sites were on an alignment. Not random.* — Karis: "Someone made this pattern." (said once; nobody answers) — **Closing, exact:** "I have ten things that aren't a Path," Cael said, eventually, to nobody in particular, "no tier, no rank, no file I can see — and five people, one of them on a route, who've walked into the quiet three times and come out." He turned it over once and let it stand. "And a line on a map that somebody drew before there was a registry to draw one." / Lira, one-armed, feeding the fire: "Then we follow it." / Brom: "After the thaw." / Karis, writing: "Noted." / Down the fire, the man who used to file reports about him watched the snow on the ferry landing with evident professional approval and said nothing, which — from him — was home. / Nothing out here had read him. At three floors older than any registry, every Path in the party had stopped at a line and his had not; a fourth had been paced from outside and not crossed. Nobody alive — least of all him — knew why. Someone had made the pattern. That was as far as anyone could say. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] [OWNER-pending #49]
