editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-208-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-209-### New canon minted (author's list; all ruled KEEP)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:210:- **Lowmarch's ground (flag):** the town on the river's east bank; a cable ferry, a square scow wound across by a drum in a round thatched capstan-shed, with a beast walking the circle; a copper a wheel and a copper a beast; the lower inn with a deep eave, above the landing; the upper inn on the rise, with two chimneys; the smith between; the meadow below, half a mile, with one great ash; standing-money a copper a night, hay by the net; the grass behind the landing. Roads out: the west road, the north water road, the east road over a saddle (a cart's width to the saddle, a mule's gauge beyond), the south road (it forks), and the cold road, which leaves the north road at a dead tree.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-211-- **The plank (flag):** twelve feet of tarred ship's oak on two posts under the lower inn's eave; slips on bark, hide, a shingle or paper, each on one tack, with a small picture beside the words for people without letters; Pike's horn ink-pot set in a bored hole; his flat river stone for the page; an iron box bolted under the plank for the hirers' coin.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-212-- **How a line is made (flag):** the price is left with Pike at posting; a crew takes a slip at the plank and Pike marks it; the job's witness marks the slip; Pike reads the line aloud before he writes it and again after, then pays. Pike's sign for the five: five short strokes. Marks seen: the ferryman's (a ring with a dot), the north-water steading's (three uprights and a bar), the hide-woman's (a square with four pegs), Thornwater's (a thorn twig over a wavy line), the landing broker's (a hook and a bar, in wax and burned on his goods).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:213:- **The wall (flag):** one sheet of sized sailcloth pinned by the lower inn's hearth, in Pike's hand, a line to a crew. Thirteen lines on day 49. One crew is entered under its mule's name (not given).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-214-- **HOLD (flag):** a captain asks Pike to keep a slip by until he is back; "Anybody can ask. I've said yes to one."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-215-- **Pike:** the left arm gone at the elbow, sleeve pinned with a brass pin; forty headings in the book; "thirty years" of the same question. His guess that the top crew's captain is Bronze, unwritten; the nearest station "nine days west".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:216:- **The sale (#23; flag):** the gelding to the ferryman, for his capstan, with dry room for the three boxes in the loft over the drum as part of the price; the old capstan mule put out to grass. The cart to the smith, who means to cut its axle to mule gauge and hire it out. Brom's bill-hook came under the cart's seat board. Lira's long knife is the last thing the Book 6 purse buys. No figure is given for the sale, the purse or the reserve.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-217-- **The reserve:** sewn into canvas by Karis, waxed by Brom, five thumbs in the wax, at the bottom of the third box under the masonry chips; opened by all five or not at all.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-218-- **The hold, as taught (flag):** the gravel bar drills; "you refuse at the first stride and at every stride after"; the word **rent** for what a fragment costs to carry idle. Karis habitually leaves set points behind her and held one unlit to ninety, later three hundred. Brom's Iron Skin comes "all or none".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-219-- **Shadow's source habit (flag):** Seln learned it on a stair as a boy; "a year to do on purpose and three more to stop doing by accident"; it came at dusk. Two drifts in Cael (day 5, four strides; day 24, one stride), logged as rent.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:220:- **Roles (all unnamed):** the courier (about fifty, a split lip long healed, a hat cut away on the right, a hatchet in a saddle loop); the three carts' people, who are one group throughout: the old carter with two mules, who takes the shade of the ash; the boy of about fifteen; the hide-woman, who is also the wash's hirer; the ferryman and his boy; the standing-money boy; the smith; the landing broker and his clerk; the old man of the north-water steading, his white dog, his goat; the Thornwater carter (short, thick, twenty-two years on his road); the steading's woman (broad, a grey braid); the bowman; the north-road woman captain (a red cloth round her hair; two men and a girl); the eleven-bale captain (a new coat).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-221-- **The road's craft:** two cairns set to mark a slanting ford; stock watered below the crossing; the stone rings on halting-grounds are for chocks, not fires; a carter's axles kept in mutton fat, trace chains bound in sacking, heel-plates cut off.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-222-- **Fauna:** red-barked conifers with flat paired needles (Karis will not name them; "red not-pine" is entered as Lira's); a broad pale tree with silver-backed leaves; grey long-legged deer with white rumps that are not afraid of people.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-226-- **Thornwater (flag):** a grain hold: river-country grain stored and fetched by carts from holds farther east. A fence of split posts as high as a man's head, a quarter of a mile about; a west gate with a bar and a platform beside it; a wicket north to grazing and a stone hut; an east gate and a road on up the valley (walked by Seln for two hours, at noon; nothing said of it); a long house, a barn with the loft over it, a cart-yard, a well with a sweep, geese.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-227-- **The carter's map (flag):** a scraped calfskin in oak-gall ink and burnt stick: roads as double lines, fords as three wavy strokes, holds as a square with a dot, Lowmarch as a ring with a bar, days as ticks, and bare hide wherever a wheel has no business. Given to Karis for the wheel Brom rebuilt. Five roads run off its edges.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:228:- **Teague, as seen (flag):** forty or so, middle height, heavy in the forearm, cropped hair grey over the ears; a black leather band laced on the right wrist; a hand-axe in his belt; a coat mended by somebody else. His week on the cold road is salt on mules to the top holds before frost shuts the pass, along two miles of ledge; he has done it nine times. He thinks only "the spear", "the bow" (a bad leg), "the boy". One other crew on the sheet could clear the ford and is up the north road.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-229-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-230-### State at movement end (author; updated after repair r1)
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-306-- **Teague:** back down the cold road on the 57th; read the struck slip twice and the five's line; took two holds' slips from the north end of the plank and went up the north water at next light. Not seen.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-307-- **The well (flag):** at the south road's fork, half a day out on level ground; a dry-stone curb, a windlass; paid from the standing-money. It went sour at the thaw; a carter's boy was drawn up asleep. Foul air lay fifteen feet deep on the water at thirty feet. Pike's line: *The well at the south fork. Air cleared, shaft drawn, six stones set. Four marks.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:308:- **Roles (all unnamed):** the hold's boy on the leaning mule; the man with the bound arm; the clouded-eyed east carter, his wife, and the small boy on her foot-board; the shingle pair; the southbound carter whose son went down the well.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-309-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-310-### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-368-### New canon minted (author's list)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-369-- **The Oxhollow slip (flag):** real paper, a careful unpractised hand, the hold's mark a horned head, broad between the horns, over three wavy strokes. *The high traverse, Oxhollow to Thornwater. To be walked with a cart, and mapped. Paid at Oxhollow, on the map: seventy marks.* No coin is left in Pike's box; the hirer pays on delivery and marks the slip.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:370:- **Why the job exists (flag):** an Oxhollow cart fetching Thornwater grain goes round by Lowmarch's ferry, eight days each way; the salt crews speak of a shelf over the high ground between, and a mule string once came over it in three days. Oxhollow is "a ford with a fence round it"; its keeper takes a copper a wheel.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-371-- **Which way it is walked (flag):** east to west. The eastern foot is at the lower of the two crossings on the Thornwater road, where a side water comes in from the north; an old cart-track, grown over, climbs it for two hours to a gorge. Thornwater is not visited and the stretch is not walked.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:372:- **The smith's terms (flag):** the cart is the party's own, sold on day 12 and cut to a mule's gauge (four feet between the wheels, five from hub to hub). Six marks laid down against its return, which is the hire; six more if it does not come back. Paid at first light on the 71st: in hand, forty-six. It is drawn by hand, two in the shafts.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-373-- **The boxes go (flag):** the ferryman is filling the loft over the drum with hay against the cold and wants all of it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-374-- **Brom's strap:** a doubled bight of the ferryman's long rope over his head and one shoulder, made fast low on the cart's near side; he draws with his chest and keeps both hands behind him. On the bench he walks on the up-slope side and leans against it. **The ferryman's rope went into the gorge with the cart.**
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-376-- **Pike's two tales (flag):** a salt string on the cold road, under a ledge herd, whose Force shifted a fallen block with his Path, and "the hill came down, with the herd upon it"; and roofing-stone cutters who used to come up the side water with carts and one year did not come back. Pike could not say which kind of loud.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-377-- **Karis's derived page (flag), as read out:** *Shale-back. Seventy-fifth day. One: it does not answer fire at three hundred and fifty yards, nor sound, nor a blow on its own shelf. Two: it answers something given off by one of its own in fright, at once, the whole herd together, by moving away. Three: by that, and by the carters' rule, it will answer a declaration in the same way, and a declaration is a great deal larger than a frightened animal. Derived. Not tested.* Copied into Cael's log in his words, with what he saw at the west end. On the map's margin it reads as derived on the seventy-fifth day and used on the seventy-eighth, and Karis will not write that it is tested, since she could not see both ends of her line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:378:- **The mountain (flag):** the fan (two hundred and sixty yards, a gully along its gorge-ward edge, rock islands; climbed in six stages); the bench (thirty feet at best, pitched outward a hand or two to the yard; slab, with tongues of loose plates where gullies cross); a stone dropped from the first hundred is heard at a count of four and a piece, and again off the far wall; four sleeping places under rock, each found by Seln; eight narrowings (eleven feet; nine; nine and a half; seven; eight; six and a hand; five feet nine with a crust at the rim; the eighth nine feet wide and broken clean across by a slot of two feet); the bay (two hundred yards by forty, floored with shale, a seep at its eastern corner); the pale rock, or fin (see the event list's amendment); the ledge (three hundred yards, six to eight feet wide, roofed in parts); the lip (thirty-one paces, four feet wide, tilted, forty-four scratched stones); the shoulder; a mule track down the western side; a valley road north-west to Oxhollow, a day and a half.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-379-- **The map (flag):** one long pasted leaf: two ruled lines for the shelf, with crosses for hollow places, hatched tongues for loose stone, a black bar at the eighth, and nothing drawn beyond the bay; beside it six columns (number, width, pitch, footing, water, and whether it takes a cart, with a reason); a separate column numbering the narrowings; the cart's own gauge in a box at the head. **Sixty-three lines**, sixty-two in Cael's hand and the last in Karis's. The verdict is Karis's last column and Pike's later line: carts go round.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-380-- **The stampede, as fixed:** see chapter 19 and the event list. Lira's burst is involuntary and is her own Path. Karis's line is nine points and eight channels, about sixty yards, held eight seconds; it empties her. Three or four heavy falls are heard after the cart; nobody sees them. From the western ledge on the 81st the herd counts twenty-five.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-381-- **Karis's lamp:** a small brass reading lantern that lives in the left-hand box with her pens.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:382:- **Oryn, as seen (flag):** not tall, square in the shoulder, broad in the hand, hair cropped as short as a boy's; a man's brown coat made for a bigger person and taken in ("off a peg that nobody was using any more", given by a hold in her first year); a low hoarse voice; a small brown mule with a pack-saddle, two panniers and a crossbow in an oiled cover lashed on top. She stops a stride and a half from people. Cael puts her at about ten years older than himself; no age is stated. Her right heel is rubbed raw and taped, and has been for two rounds.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-383-- **Tide, as taught (flag):** contact only. What mends is the patient's own current, which stands at a break "like water behind a board"; she finds where it stands, opens the way with her own, and holds it open while the body does six weeks' knitting in under an hour, and she pays for the six weeks. A reserve "like a purse", spent at the rate of what it mends: three mendings in a day if she has slept under a roof and been fed, two on a road. She will not touch a table until she has eaten and slept two hours. She cannot do it to herself. She mends what she can read. **The surface reading:** hands on the hurt, or two fingers on a wrist and two on the neck, for a count of ten; it costs her nothing she would notice. **The deep reading ("the long one"):** both hands, all of her, minutes, the patient still and whole, at a mending's cost; not run on a road. A person's current runs in a bed, and "the shape of the bed is their Path"; she names Karis as Ember by it. **The stall:** a hand on a wrist for a breath as the other means to declare, and the declaration does not come; it costs a day's mendings and the next day's and mends nobody; she has done it and hates it. No count of times is given.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-384-- **Tape (flag):** linen strip three fingers wide, spread with pitch, mutton fat and something from a hold that keeps bees. Five bands from breastbone to spine, laid on the out-breath. Twenty-one days from the 78th; she means to lift it herself. For Lira's ankle: an anchor turn above the joint, two strips under the heel and up the outside, and a figure of eight.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-385-- **Brom's wrist:** mended on the 80th; a cuff of plain linen "to remind the hand"; a week from the middle of that day: it takes what sits on it and nothing that hangs from it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:386:- **Oryn's route, as told (flag):** seven holds, twenty days, "thirty-odd" rounds; late eleven times and this the twelfth, five days behind; nobody has put a coin in her hand past the Line; holds feed her and the mule, one shoes the mule, one gave the coat. She began with four holds and added the fifth in her third round, the sixth "for an old woman's sake" and the seventh because of a child. In a city she was one of six on a healing house's staff, where the morning list is kept by tier. No city is named.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-387-- **The carter's hand:** the carter who told her of the late crew, at the foot of the lip, had a split palm that she had promised to do that evening; he hauls to Thornwater.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-388-- **Oxhollow (flag):** on the north bank of a broad shallow river, in a hollow, behind a palisade of split logs with a gate on the south side toward the ford and another on the north; a ford of a hundred yards of gravel under a foot of water; a yoke of red oxen with a chain, for drawing carts through; the keeper's low stone house with a turf roof between the gate and the water; a long house; a well; the healer's table of scrubbed ash on two trestles under a lean-to against the gate-house, with a bench along the wall. The keeper is old, bent, with a notched hazel tally-stick, and cannot read; he keeps his coin under a hearthstone. He would have sent three carts over the top at the next dry spell with a Force walking behind.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-389-- **Roles (all unnamed):** the smith; the ferryman's boy; Oxhollow's keeper; the woman who keeps Oxhollow's gate; the woman with the scald, the ox-driver, the boy with the collarbone, and five others on the bench; the man with the shoulder, the nursing mother and the old herdsman at the next hold; the child and its mother at the hold after; the carter with the split hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:390:- **Teague (flag):** two holds' work in four weeks, a drain cut and a byre roofed; two mules. The bow's limp is an old hip that went out and seated itself wrong, ten years or more ago. Teague timed his second slip to meet the healer's round at the upper hold on the 81st and waited a day. On the hill above Oxhollow he asks her whether the hip is a thing she would do ("Not on a road. Not in a night."), and she tells him his five are in the yard ("They're not mine." / "No. They're not anybody's. I noticed that.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-391-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-392-### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:393:*Updated after repair r1 (see `REPAIR-REPORT-r1.md`) and the coordinator's ten audit fixes. Facts changed: Teague knows only that the healer was late, not why, and cannot set his lost day against the five; Brom's older ash wedge was not lost and lies with the three boxes; Oryn's sum now reads whole on the 99th, the long reading on the 100th at the earliest, four days of work at Thornwater's table beyond her stop and one day put on the route; Seln asks leave to go ahead and leaves scratched pebbles for word, and finds a clawless footmark at the first seep; Oryn washes her hands before she kneels, and checks her hands on Brom's wrist in the middle of the first reading; the ankle is asked for from the mule's back on the morning of the 82nd; chapter 18 has three scenes. Word counts, metrics, line numbers and flags elsewhere in this report are the pre-repair figures; the movement now stands at 41,346 words.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-394-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-395-**Calendar.** Dusk on the **eighty-fourth day past the Line**, on Oxhollow's bank. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("the cold term" twice; "frost"; "the next dry spell"). Days on the page: 70, 71, 72, 73, 74, 75, 76, 77, 78, 79, 80, 81, 82, 83 (in passing), 84; and, in Oryn's window only, 86, 89, 91 and 92. Teague's window is marked as the eighty-fourth day still. Weather: dry roads; first ice on a kettle on the 74th and frost on the bench each morning after; a cold rain on the 79th; milder in the valley. The next movement opens on Oxhollow's bank at dusk on the 84th, or the morning after.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-396-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:397:**Where everyone is.** The five are at Oxhollow, in the yard and at the ford, with three boxes on the ground against the gate-house wall. Oryn has gone north out of the gate at dusk with her mule, and is due at Thornwater on the 93rd. Teague and his three have crossed the ford southward at dusk with two mules, a day ahead of the five on the Lowmarch road.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-398-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-399-**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** **Deployment since the Line: one** (the ford burst, day 53). Nothing was used on the mountain or since: Anchor, Compression, the Iron read, Wind and Storm all offered and were refused; Shadow sealed. **Three ribs broken, left side, low, on the 78th; taped with five bands on the 81st; twenty-one days from the break, and Oryn means to lift the tape herself.** Left calf opened along the old bite on the 78th, bound in Oryn's linen, not mended. No log entries for the 78th and 79th. He has been read three times by a healer (the 80th, and twice on the 84th) and has answered three questions truly: his hurts knit in the right places; faster than other people's; no healer has ever got anything from him. He has not asked Oryn south. He has not answered Hesk's letter. Teague has spoken to him and he has said one word.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-400-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:401:**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. **One involuntary full burst on the 78th**, when the ledge went (her body travelled about twenty feet; the declaration and its crack crossed the gorge); a second refused, six yards short of shelter. **Right tibia broken on the 78th, set and mended on the 80th: straight, new, to walk within the week and not to be run on for a month.** **Right ankle never mended** ("That's a tape and a season. It'll set."); she asked once, from the mule's back, on the 82nd; she tapes it herself as Oryn taught her and says that she now knows where it is. Her right boot is under the mountain; she is barefoot on that side. She rode Oryn's mule from the shoulder to Oxhollow and has not said the word.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-402-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-403-**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. No declaration; the Skin did not start under the cart at the eighth narrowing. **Left forearm opened at the wrist on the 78th (two boxes), mended on the 80th; in a linen cuff; a week from the middle of the 80th, to take what sits on it and nothing that hangs from it.** He carried the third box down the mountain on his back. He has the hedging bill and the older ash wedge.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-409-**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four, said by herself. She knows that she cannot read Cael, by surface reading, hurt or whole, and that his ribs knit "with nothing doing it"; she knows nothing of fragments and has no theory. She has promised him the long reading "when you're not broken". **Her sum (her window, the 92nd):** whole on the 99th by the rule, though her hands say sooner; the long reading on the 100th at the earliest; her Thornwater stop ends on the 95th; she means to work four days more at Thornwater's table and has put one day on the route, for the reading. She is five days behind her round. She has mended six times on the page: Lira's leg and Brom's wrist (80th); a scald, a foot and a collarbone (84th); and, in her window, a shoulder at two mendings' cost (86th). She keeps no record. She told Teague on the hill only that she was late.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-410-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:411:**Teague.** At Oxhollow's ford at dusk on the 84th he said his four things and crossed. He knows: no cart; a wrist in a healer's cuff; the girl's foot strapped; the small one asleep sitting up; the boy's ribs taped; that the mountain came down and all five came off it, mostly on their feet; that the keeper paid seventy for a no. **He knows that the healer was late to the upper hold on the 81st, where he had waited a day for the bow's hip, and he does not know why; he has not connected it with the five.** He does not know what Cael is. He and his three (the spear, the bow, the boy) and two mules are a day ahead on the road south.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-412-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-413-**Objects and money.** **The cart is in the gorge**, with the ferryman's rope, the blankets, the kettle, the canvas and the flour. Three boxes, whole, and Brom's ash wedge beside them; the reserve sealed in the third, unopened. Seln's case. Hesk's satchel, with the log, the old volume, the notebook, Hesk's letter and Pike's lines on bark. Karis's lantern, cord, brass straightedge and Hesk's clock. Board purse: **a hundred and thirty-two marks earned** (62 + Oxhollow 70); **a hundred and sixteen in hand**; **six owed to the smith** for the cart. Pike's slip is in hand, with five strokes and Oxhollow's mark at its foot, to be carried to the plank. The long leaf was unrolled on the keeper's board and paid for there; the text does not say who carries it away, and the keeper is its buyer.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-427-- Brom's left wrist is mended under the day-80-to-day-87 rule: it may take what sits on it, nothing hanging from it, and he must release a pulling load. His hedging bill and the older ash wedge survive (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:3-5,267-277`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:37-43`; fix 10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-428-- Cael's three left-low ribs were broken day 78 and received five bands on day 81, to be lifted on day 99 by Oryn if possible; his reopened calf is only cloth-bound. His nine fragments are held, Shadow remains sealed, and deployment since the Line is one (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:121-155`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:3-45`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:325-333`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:429:- Oryn has failed three surface readings of Cael, knows only that he heals fast with no readable current, knows nothing of fragments, has run no deep reading, keeps no written record, and has put one day on her route for the promised whole-and-still reading (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:317-351`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:53-89,137-155,211-233`). Her mule still carries her panniers and covered crossbow; do not spend owner decision #24 early (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:143-159`; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:103-107`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-430-- After fixes 6–9, Teague knows only what his own schedule and the yard/keeper show: he missed Oryn on day 81; on day 84 the five have no cart, have healer-made bindings, delivered a paid no, and all survived. He does not know they caused Oryn's lateness and knows nothing of fragments or the mechanism (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:237-295`; fixes 6–9).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-431-- The three boxes are whole at Oxhollow; the reserve is sealed in the third. The marked Oxhollow slip must return to Pike. The long map leaf was paid for on the keeper's board; the keeper is its buyer. Seln's closed case remains on its strap, and Hesk's satchel still carries the log, old volume, notebook, Hesk letter, and Pike's bark lines (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:153`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:27-37,89-93`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:321-361`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:323-327`).
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-454-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-455-### New canon minted (author's list)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:456:- **Oxhollow's grain cart (flag).** Since his carts "go round", the keeper sends one to Thornwater for grain on the 85th, eight days out and eight home. Its carter is his sister's son: a long, sleepy-faced young man with very large feet and two grey mules, who says about forty words in six days. The three boxes ride his bed from Oxhollow to Thornwater (85th–93rd) for nothing, because the five walk his road in front of him. No paper, no line. He rests the 91st at Lowmarch and loads grain at Thornwater on the 94th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:457:- **Lira's boot.** The carter's spare pair, each "as long as Cael's forearm"; he will not split a pair; two marks. She packs the right with a torn shirt over her taped foot; the left hangs from the cart's tail, is left at Thornwater's barn door by the carter, and goes east on Oryn's mule "against the other one going".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-458-- **The road Oxhollow–Lowmarch (flag):** south down a broad valley of alder and rough pasture, small fords, halting-grounds; on the fourth day two hundred yards of moss crossed by a causeway of laid logs (the carter's father's), about one log in six rotten at the heart. It reaches Lowmarch's river on the west bank and crosses by the ferry.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:459:- **Teague's crew on a road:** single file, a crew's length apart; no fire at any halt; chock-stones left as found; the mules at the windward end.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-460-- **The ferryman's rope (flag):** sixty yards of four-strand, laid up by himself. He will take no silver ("a figure's a thing you can pay and walk off from"); he will have a rope when they have one. Entered by Karis as owed, with no price.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-461-- **The two HOLD slips (flag):** one bark and one shingle; a bull to be brought down off top grazing before the snow, and a ford to be staked. Each hold "asked who". They will wait a fortnight for the five and then have Teague. Cael tells Pike on the 91st not to keep them past the fortnight. **They are still on the oak at the end of the movement.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-462-- **How the posting came (flag):** by the last mail-ferry, to the landing broker, sealed, with a hundred marks in a bag and "a line of direction"; the broker's clerk brought it up the next morning. Pike said it twice that day to forty people, nobody scratched, and he has kept it under his stone since ("A thing on a tack is a thing I'm offering."). The clerk is the hirer's witness: whatever is brought down is to be seen at the landing, marked, and sent west by the next boat. He does not know what the things are or who wants them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-463-- **The posting as an object (flag), by Seln:** cream paper of an office's weight; a margin pricked with a wheel; "Recovery." set alone as a heading; the sum in words and again in a bracket; the place described and not named.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:464:- **The wall on the 90th:** the five are tenth; one of the two crews they passed is four people, none young, one with a wooden foot, who brought a mule string through the cold road's pass and lost none.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-465-- **Pike's rule for a job with nothing at the end of it:** "I write what was done… if his mark never goes on it, the box stays shut."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-466-- **Eleven witnesses on the 91st:** Teague and his three; the Oxhollow carter; the hide-woman; the old carter under the ash; the shingle pair; the standing-money boy; the broker's clerk.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-468-- **The registry's printed sheet (flag):** east of the Line it shows a river or two without their bends, hills drawn alike, and seven dashed roads with no names that run out into white and stop; the third from the top crosses the first water (no ferry, no Lowmarch) and ends three fingers east of it, at about Thornwater's fence or an hour beyond. **"Void"** (flag): Seln says that in a registry's usage an entry is void when nothing is written against it, and supposes that a carter was once shown such a sheet.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-469-- **Three blank circles on the carter's map (flag; see owner flag 4):** the bend east of Thornwater, and two round blanks that Karis had read as thrift, one in his hill-hatching a day south of Lowmarch and a little aside, one far to the south-east among his water-strokes with no road within a day. She rings all three in pencil and writes *guess* beside two. The hide is "a map of days" and will not take a straightedge.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:470:- **Oryn at Thornwater (flag):** she mends the carter's split palm on a plank inside the west gate before she eats ("That's one."). Her changed plan: she had meant to sit at this gate's table until the 99th; she walks the Fallow road in those days, the same six gates waiting the same days; Thornwater's bench "goes short" and is to be paid on her way back. She has been round the ring "thirty times, with the mule, by the ruts" (her round goes on east by that road). The carters' saying, as given: *You'll not want her in the ring; she's no good there.*, first heard at the first gate she ever mended at.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-471-- **Karis's reserve:** her first point since the 78th is set on a lamp-wick in Thornwater's yard on the 93rd, at Oryn's bidding; "three parts full".
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-472-- **The long cord:** two box-ropes spliced by Brom, stretched from a fence-post, marked off with red wool against the short cord. **Its length is never stated**, nor is Karis's stride.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-476-- **Hound sign outside:** three runs through the grass within twenty yards of each other on the eastern side, crossing the line both ways; none on the north side.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-477-- **What each of the five reports inside** (beyond the protected lines): Karis can see where sixteen points would go and "can't find the hand to reach with"; this is not being empty ("reserve present, sigil gone"). Brom: "There's no next room"; a hundredweight weighs the same. Seln: "It is not there to be asked." Lira: a yard and a half, and no crack. Oryn: the surface count stops at "Four—"; returns at the stride; and stops when she alone is inside with Brom's wrist held across the line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:478:- **The mule** grazes across the stone with two feet either side and is not troubled.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-479-- **The floor (flag):** on the crown of a low swell, twenty-six of Cael's strides across by two diameters; colder than the turf; soundless under a boot; its rim rolled over like the rim of a dish, a hand above the turf outside and a finger above the floor within; level under a taut cord and under the brass and thread. Eleven squared grey uprights stand a stride in from the rim, each as thick as a man's body, the tallest twice Brom's height and the shortest knee-high. Round each, at chest height, and round the inner face of the lip, a band a hand wide of fine sunk lines, straight, hooked and crossing. None of Karis's forty-odd chips matches.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-480-- **The rubbings (flag):** one sheet to an upright, pencil rubbed over paper held flat by Lira; ten whole and the eleventh half done; numbered, with each stone's height and facing. They are in the middle box (the eleventh rolled inside Karis's coat).
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-487-**Calendar.** Sunset on the **ninety-sixth day past the Line**, at the eastern lip of the Fallow Ring's floor. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("the cold term"; "frost"; "before the snow"; "fortnight"). Days on the page: 84 (dusk), 85, 86, 87, 88, 89, 90, 91, 92, 93, 94, 95, 96; and, in Teague's window, the evening of the 89th. Weather: frost every morning; dry roads; a north wind on the Fallow. The next movement opens where this one stops.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-488-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:489:**Where everyone is.** Six people at the den under the eastern lip, ten cords and half a floor inside the line: Cael, Lira, Brom (with the middle box on his back), Karis (with the eleventh sheet rolled in her coat), Seln (on one knee, the locked case on its strap across his chest) and Oryn. The lane trodden by the cord runs from the floor's western lip two hundred yards and more down to the grey stone. Oryn's mule is hobbled on the western side of the stone with her panniers, six of Thornwater's blankets, the carter's left boot and the long shape in its oiled cover still lashed on the pack. No hound has been seen. The sun is half under the hills.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-490-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-491-**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** Logged deployment since the Line: one (the ford); the day-96 entry carries no deployment line. **On the 96th, unwitnessed:** the Iron read opened a pace short of the line and carried across it; a foot's worth of Wind evasion twenty strides inside; the Iron read once more on the floor. Shadow is sealed and untouched; it lifted at dusk on the 95th at the turn of the ruts and on the 96th inside the line, and was refused both times. Anchor asked at the stone and at the stake. Ribs: taped, eighteen days from the break, three to go. Calf: bound in Oryn's linen, closing by itself. He has told nobody that anything answered him inside, and has given Karis "It was dark before… It's dark now." for her sixth row. Hesk's satchel holds the log, the old volume, the notebook, Hesk's letter, Pike's lines on bark, and now Ephram's letter and Vell's. He has not answered any of the three.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-521-- **Live Arbiter result:** Karis, Brom, Seln, Lira and Oryn fail at the same step; Cael's Arbiter was already dark and remains described only that way. Oryn knows no fragment mechanism (`manuscript/chapter-27.md:189-229`; `manuscript/chapter-29.md:181-233,283-297`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-522-- **Hounds are still sign only:** Seln reads eight or nine fresh outward tracks to the east and none back; M5 may make the packet's nine visible, but no M4 character has yet seen one (`manuscript/chapter-30.md:155-193`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:18,24`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:523:- **Exact party/object placement:** six at the den; Brom wears the middle box; Seln is on one knee; Oryn's mule is hobbled west of the line stone with two panniers, six borrowed blankets, the unused left boot and covered crossbow; two boxes remain in Thornwater, with the reserve sealed in the third (`manuscript/chapter-27.md:13-29`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:3-7,219-239`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:167,183`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-524-- **Site evidence:** no instruments were found on the floor or within forty yards; stake 31 is registry-stamped, about five years weathered and untouched; the eleven uprights carry unknown bands round their feet (no band on the lip) [corrected at M4 close]; Karis's chips match nothing (`manuscript/chapter-28.md:107-143,219-235`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:53-123`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-525-- **Maps and withheld memory:** Karis's calfskin has three circles, two marked *guess*; the registry sheet has seven dashed roads and the Fallow is the third. Seln has not yet supplied his map-memory inference; that remains M5's (`manuscript/chapter-26.md:109-149`; `MOVEMENT-004.md:54-56`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:25-26`).
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-537-- **Deployment since the Line: THIRTEEN.** One at the ford (day 53) and twelve in the Ring on the night of the 96th, each priced and billed in the night log: Iron read; Shadow (once, ten strides); Wind; Pressure; Ember (one point on the knife's tip); Blade (an edge on Lira's knife); Anchor (perception only — a deliberate release counts); Storm lanes one, two and three (ten / ten / twelve counts; the body read lost while the air is held); Wind a second time; Compression at contact, late. The two noon tests of the 96th are left out of the number, unexplained. All capability rules held.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-538-- **Shadow has been used ONCE and remains sealed.** Only Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln had the sightline; Oryn was screened and saw him arrive, not come; the pack is no witness. Oryn cannot identify Seln as its source. Seln struck Cael's second reason for silence ("I shall not be a reason… I should sooner have her told what may be done to her than be used to keep her ignorant") WITHOUT offering to be known as the source: Movement 6 tells her sources by Path, not by person, and the seal serves again at the Stair.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:539:- **The Ring:** nine hounds counted on the white; two dead by Brom's bolts (thirteen feet; six feet); seven away "north and south along the line's outside", direction unobserved. The crossbow was on the mule; Seln fetched it during the retreat round the floor and Brom spanned it by hand. Bolts: six, five in the sleeve from the 97th. Geometry as closed in Movement 4.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-540-- **Inside the line** no companion Path was used: Oryn's hands had nothing ("Nothing in my hands"); cloth and knees. Nobody has theorized why the fragments answered. *Quieting* has still not been said. "Compact" has been said aloud once, by Seln. Nothing is known of where the file is, what it says or why; dating stops at "five years… maybe six". Seln's map memory (maps with holes) is open; he asked for the carter's map.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-541-- **The tenth fragment — Tide-adjacent — was acquired on the 100th** in Oryn's long reading (minute twenty-one); the notice is exact; "More than one" is said. **Cael let it happen without telling her first, with the covenant written beforehand, and told her the minute it was over. The page treats it as a wrong he did knowingly**: all four companions named it for what it is, he agreed that refusing would be right, and he chose against it. Writing it first made it knowing, not permitted. Oryn does NOT yet know the mechanism: her own naming of what was done, her terms and its cost to him are Movement 6's first scene. Integration cost is not yet paid.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-564-- **The posting read as a question:** by Seln, as inference: a paper that sends a crew to fetch what is not there asks only what becomes of the crew; the broker's clerk is to send word west by the next boat.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-565-- **Thornwater:** five on the bench under the back room's window on the 99th, one a man who cut his shin with a scythe "at the start of the harvest"; she reads all five and puts them off until after noon on the 100th. The back room: one window in the eastern wall with a shutter, a bench under it, a scrubbed plank on two trestles, a three-legged stool, a peg on a thong for a latch; her things on a strip of canvas along the sill (tape on its stick, flask, shears, linen, horn cup, bone needle). The bowman takes off his cap when Lira comes in slung.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:566:- **Oryn's route:** "the top gate of my round's eleven days north of here", by the road, at the mule's pace. No lateness figure is given.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-567-- **Karis's page:** a single leaf, two years in the making: a curve for how quickly each fragment came, a column for what each cost afterward, and three words at its head. She calls it a model.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-568-- **Small things:** Karis's lantern holds "three fingers" of oil after the hour and "a finger" in the loft. Seln makes Brom's bread to dictation and it does not burn. One of Thornwater's six blankets is returned a hand narrower. Lira climbs the loft ladder with her right hand and both knees.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-569-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-570-### State at movement end (author; governed by the rulings above and by the surviving prose)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:571:*Updated after repair r1 (see `REPAIR-REPORT-r1.md`). Facts changed: Brom's hurt is ONE hand, four finger-pads; Oryn's rule for it is "Nothing on the string for three days"; Seln strikes Cael's second reason without offering to be known to Oryn; Lira's arm was first bound with Brom's folded cuff and strips of Oryn's shirt, her linen being on the mule; Cael's calf stays in Karis's blanket strip from the 96th until the yard on the 99th and is never bound by Oryn; the hound that Cael throws is let go by and helped on its way, after the jaws are levered open with the hilt of Lira's knife; the second lock is struck from behind, and he goes down onto the left forearm. Word counts, metrics and line numbers elsewhere in this report are the pre-repair figures; the markers it lists are filled.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-572-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-573-**Calendar.** The morning of the **hundredth day past the Line**, in Thornwater's back room, in the twenty-first minute of the long reading. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("first snow", "the snow", "the harvest", "frost"). Days on the page: 96 (sunset to night), 97, 98, 99, 100. Weather: frost every night; a north wind on the Fallow; ice on Thornwater's trough.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-574-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:575:**Where everyone is.** Cael on the plank table with Oryn's hands on him, the door shut. Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln in or about the loft over the barn, with all three boxes and the covenant leaf in Hesk's book. The mule in Thornwater's yard. Five of the hold's people waiting until after noon.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-576-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-577-**Cael.** Eighteen. **Ten confirmed fragments** from the twentieth minute: the tenth is Tide-adjacent, partial, Iron, self and contact, *Acquisition: directed. Engagement: clinical — non-hostile.* It has not been tried, and its cost has not begun. The uncounted anomaly is untouched and unmentioned in this movement. **Deployment since the Line: thirteen** (the ford; twelve in the Ring on the 96th), as his log has it; the noon tests of the 96th are noted in the log as left out. Shadow used **once**. Ribs whole, the tape off on the 99th. Calf closed; it stayed in Karis's blanket strip from the night of the 96th until Oryn undid the knot in the yard on the 99th. Left forearm bruised and working (he came down on it under the hound's weight in the second lock). He knows that refusing would have been right and that the leaf permitted nothing; he chose against it and means to answer for it. He has told Oryn two things: that what she saw on the hill was his doing, and, in the last minute, "I need to tell you what I am." He has told nobody why anything answered him inside, and has not told Lira since when he knew. Three letters still unanswered.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-587-**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. Three mendings on the crew in two days; none since. She has crossed the line eight times alone at dawn on the 98th, which only Cael saw. She has read him five times at the surface and once at depth, and has found movement, "more than one", and no banks. She felt something change in him in the twentieth minute; she has been told that he did it and that he must tell her what he is; **she does not know the mechanism**. Thornwater's bench is owed four days and is put off until after noon.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-588-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:589:**Objects and money.** Board purse unchanged: **a hundred and thirty-two earned; a hundred and eight in hand.** The Fallow hundred lies in Pike's box; no instruments were found; the posting (five strokes) is in Hesk's book. The crossbow, with **five bolts**, is with the crew; its spanning hook is in the mule's near-side pannier. One bolt lies on the Ring's floor. Six blankets returned, one a hand narrow. The rope is still owed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-590-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-591-**Hounds.** Nine came; two are dead (one on the floor, one drawn off a hundred yards south of the stone, outside the line); **seven went north and south along the line's outside** on the night of the 96th and were not seen, tracked or heard again.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-598-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-599-### Next-movement inheritance (Sol plan audit §8; also written into the next packet)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:600:Movement 6 already carries the telling, birthday, Quieting name, tables, shooting lessons, mule decision, cash after the birthday, string-ban expiry and Oryn's northward window (`MOVEMENT-006.md:20-53`). Its author must additionally inherit these surviving-prose facts:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-601-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:602:- **Brom/crossbow:** one hand has four mended string-lines; the restriction ends on day 100; the bow has five bolts, while the spanning hook remains in the mule's near pannier (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:15-21,53`; fixes 2–7, 9–11, 14, 16–17 and 19). The long knife is blunt from Blade's bill (`manuscript/chapter-33.md:211-213`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-603-- **Bodies:** Lira's left arm remains slung and under the no-hold/no-strike/no-catch order; her right ankle is unmended and she must walk flat; her mended tibia is not to be run on until about day 110 (`manuscript/chapter-33.md:101-125`; `manuscript/chapter-35.md:63-69,155-215`). Cael's ribs and calf are whole, but the left forearm has sensation only as far as the wrist on day 99 (`manuscript/chapter-35.md:265-329`). Karis has only rough single words (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:9`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-604-- **Counts/seal:** deployment since the Line is thirteen; Shadow has been used once and remains sealed; Oryn cannot identify Seln as its source and must hear sources by Path, not person (`manuscript/chapter-33.md:203-233`; fix 18; `MOVEMENT-006.md:26`).
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-622-- **Karis's five findings** stand as scenes; she does not know the strokes are letters, counts kinds and will not number them from one site; the bands were rubbed a hand above the floor; identical failure across five sigils (Iron R1, Copper, Iron R3, Bronze, Iron R4). Karis is Ember, Iron Rank Three.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-623-- **Pike's Fallow copy** came by carter ("Six went in. Six came out."), set against Cael's MEMORY of Gault's line; no leaf of Gault's is carried. Hesk's package did not come with it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:624:- **Oryn:** stayed five extra days for one slow mark on Lira's arm; "sixteen out of this gate"; left by the northern wicket at first light on the 111th in the protected words ("North in the morning… three days north by the time you're back at the board… Thornwater's on my route"). Her mule is with the crew (#24). She will be at Millrace on the 113th (EXC-B7-003, owner-resolved: her circuit brings her round).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-625-- **"Tomorrow makes three"** (the protected second pole, ch44) stands verbatim and unglossed: OWNER-DECISIONS #51.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-626-- **Bodies:** Lira one-armed, shooting; Brom's string restriction ended on the 100th and the crossbow is on his belt; Cael whole. **New canon KEEP:** the founding stone from Ostrand's old gate; the hold's yard crossbow; the husband and the hold's boy (unnamed). **Names:** none minted. **Vastin:** one window, three sentences, no age.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-651-- **Lira's arm (flag):** on the 106th seven of the eight marks have taken and the eighth, the lowest of the outer row, is slow; nothing is mended; on the 110th all eight have taken. The tibia is released on the 110th; the ankle stays taped and flat.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-652-- **Oryn's lateness (flag):** nine late at Thornwater and eleven at the next on the 104th (meaning to go on the 106th); she stays to read the arm at the fortnight; "sixteen out of this gate… A round never gives a day back; it takes one." (the 110th, in the yard); "Oxhollow's seventeen days late and the old woman's knee doesn't care what's under a floor" (the loft, the protected line), and in her window the odd day is the old woman's knee and Oxhollow is the 121st. Her window: the child was last heard on the 89th, looked for on the 109th, and cannot be heard before the 126th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:653:- **The mule (C2, flag):** left with the crew on the 110th. She goes on the low side of nothing and the driver on the low side of her; she will not cross moving water with anybody on her near hand; her near hind has been shod since the Oxhollow road; she answers to a click; she has never had a name and is not to be given one. Oryn takes the off pannier on her own back and the spare rope, thirty feet of three-strand, for the next gate's jenny.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-654-- **In the loft:** Karis asks Oryn for a healer's count at the next edge, as she had at the first; Oryn answers with her route (north at first light; three days north by the time they are back at the board; Thornwater is on her route) and with "Don't go in without me"; if it is sooner than Thornwater, they are to ask a carter which gate she is late at.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-655-- **The four wheres:** the Fallow Ring; the blank a day south of the ferry (*guess*); the blank far to the south-east among the water-strokes (*guess*); Seln's second round, unplaced.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-660-**Calendar.** Dusk on the **hundred and twelfth day past the Line** in Oryn's window; first light on the **hundred and eleventh** for the five, at Thornwater's well. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("the cold term", "frost", "the thaw", "the snow", "the harvest", "fortnight"; "Third-day" twice, as the academy's word). Days on the page: 100, 101, 102, 103, 104, 105, 106, 107, 108, 109, 110, 111 (dawn); and, in Oryn's second window, 111 and 112. Weather: hard frost every night; ice on the trough, frozen through on the 110th; no snow. The next movement opens at Thornwater on the morning of the 111th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-661-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:662:**Where everyone is.** The five at Thornwater, about to go out by the western gate with three boxes on Oryn's mule. Oryn two days north and west, on foot, a little short of a mill at dusk on the 112th.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-663-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-664-**Cael.** **Nineteen** since the middle of the meal on the 102nd. **Ten confirmed fragments.** The tenth (Tide-adjacent) has been used on himself only: three days of listening, idle by the third night; one self-reading on the night of the 102nd. He has found **a place near the middle of himself that does not flow**, which all ten go round; he knows where it is, that nothing moves in it, and that none goes through; he has not named it, has not gone back to it, and has told nobody what it is. He has told Lira and then the six that there is a thing, and that it is the healer's to hear first. The three standing words are retired; the log reads *Patience is over; observation begins.* **Deployment since the Line: thirteen**; eleven leans of Wind in the yard on the 101st are logged as practice outside the number. Shadow unused; it lifts at dusk and is refused. Body whole: ribs, calf; the left forearm's feeling back to the knuckles on the 100th, a yellow mark. He has said to Oryn that it was wrong; he has not been forgiven. **He owes her:** three readings of himself on three different days, and then all of it at once; he does not know what she would have said at the door and never will; the size of the rest is hers. **The rule** is in his book in his hand, with her note under it. He has told the six that he knew at noon on the 96th. He holds a hypothesis that he has not written. Three letters still unanswered.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md-672-**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. Unmarked. He has said that six sigils were on the road and five went out, and that he is counting it; that the west knows that something turns Paths off and does not know that something does not, "yet"; and that the record is kept. He said the birthday aloud. **Oryn has not been told that he is a source; she laid a hand on his shoulder on the 110th and said nothing. The case is on its strap, on him, shut.**
