    46	- **The walk (121–122):** frost that rings; one cart of hides and a lifted hand; holds shut; the six catalogued because they will be five; the first night in a ruined hold's lee ("Twice." / "Twice." / "And not three."). **The fork:** "three weeks late there… I'm going back to being the route." He walks her fifty paces and does not ask. "Find me at Thornwater." / "Bring the map." **The four behind him, with one mule.** The log at the fork (protected).
