292:## B. Findings affecting later movements
294:### B1. The “whole year” closing frame is impossible on the plan’s own day spine
300:**Edition evidence:** the plan opens on day 131 and closes on day 308 (`BOOK_MAP.md:19,21,88`), about 177 days. The edition does not define a short year that would make this “the whole year”; OWNER #35/#42/#48 forbid using unresolved calendar structure to repair it.
304:### B2. “First words to the six in a year” is unsupported and conflicts with the Book 8 span
310:**Edition evidence:** Teague’s tall woman is unnamed and silent toward the five in planned Book 7/Book 8 scenes, but no edition canon establishes a one-year interval. The whole Book 8 plan is only about 177 days.
314:### B3. Lira’s age-sixteen wall history is unsupported
324:### B4. Brom’s advancement review is already closed
334:### B5. Seln’s three different spans need explicit separation
340:**Edition evidence:** Seln served fifteen years; his locked case has been carried twelve years. The protected Book 7 line “Six years I’ve wanted a face” stays unglossed under OWNER #50; Book 7 also dates the survey at “five years ago by the stake, maybe six” (`OWNER-DECISIONS.md:159–162`; B7 `BOOK_MAP.md:21,309,314`).
348:### B6. “Forty years” is correct for Vastin; an age must never appear
356:**Amendment:** keep all `forty years` career lines. At `BOOK_MAP.md:436`, replace the meta sentence that repeats `53` with: `No numeric age for Vastin appears in plan, packet, narration or dialogue; “forty years” is career length only.` This prevents an apply seat from treating 53 as allowable metadata.
358:### B7. The plan’s Tide consent language must remain ask-first, not form-first
364:**Edition evidence:** “ask first, every time” is in Oryn’s and Cael’s hands (`chapter-44.md:157`; B7 `BOOK_MAP.md:32,286`). Oryn’s previous lack of consent is not repaired after the fact (`B7 ledger:616`).
