+REPAIR — chapters 53–60 require protected-text restoration, a corrected final deployment count of twenty-seven, restoration of Teague's forfeited four-mark slip, strict outside-only treatment of the fourth site, removal of extra maker/intent assertions, and one ending-object clarification. The movement's structure, calendar, bodies, money, letters, knowledge limits, and protected closing otherwise ratify.
+
+# 1. Continuity with the closed text
+
+## Contradictions requiring repair
+
+1. **Teague's four-mark weir slip was forfeited, not completed or paid.** Closed Movement 7 leaves the third stake unset and says the job costs the four marks (`manuscript/chapter-51.md:307-325`); its CLOSED ledger repeats that Teague “took and forfeited” the slip (`STATE_LEDGER.md:750-752,772`). Movement 8 instead says that he set it, that the witness marked it, and that four marks were in his belt (`manuscript/chapter-56.md:71-75`). Fix 8 restores the closed state. His day's posts on the forty-mark fence remain open and are correctly offered to the five (`manuscript/chapter-59.md:241-247`).
+
+2. **The deployment ledger cannot count the day-118 Anchor trial.** The closed baseline is twenty-three (`manuscript/chapter-51.md:217`; `manuscript/chapter-52.md:357`). The draft counts the trial as twenty-four (`manuscript/chapter-53.md:387-389`), then logs three Hall deployments as twenty-seven (`manuscript/chapter-55.md:155-163`) and the permitted Tide reading as twenty-eight (`manuscript/chapter-55.md:297-301`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:31`). But the protected inventory says Anchor was used **twice** in the year, “once each way”: the Stair unbinding and the Hall holding (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:35-41`; source `chapter-24.md:65-71`). Counting the kerb trial would make three. Fixes 1–2 and 6–8 treat the trial like the edition's excluded practice/tests and produce the only count compatible with the protected inventory: 23 → 24 read-under-water → 25 Compression → 26 Hall Anchor → 27 Tide. The self-readings remain outside the deployment count (`manuscript/chapter-55.md:169-211`), and Shadow is not used in this movement; its closed total remains twice (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:37`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:760,787`).
+
+3. **The fourth site's present staging tests the boundary and therefore spends a withheld fact.** Lira puts her boot at the iron, says “Gone,” steps back, and says “Back” (`manuscript/chapter-58.md:149-153`); Cael then treats himself as known immune there (`manuscript/chapter-58.md:159-161`). That establishes an effect on a Path even if prose later says nobody crossed. The binding ending requires the site not entered and its Path effect unknown (`BOOK_MAP.md:43`; `packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:51-60`). Fixes 13–15 stop Lira one pace above the iron, take the line from the cordon itself, and leave every body and Path outside and untested.
+
+4. **Three authored passages exceed the permitted maker language.** Karis's private window says the test “had been set for her” (`manuscript/chapter-57.md:71-73`); Cael says somebody set three floors in a row (`manuscript/chapter-58.md:109-111`); the cordon prose assigns a wish that the line be found (`manuscript/chapter-58.md:185`). Fixes 9, 12, and 17 retain the observations without agency or intent. The authored site-origin sentences that remain are exactly “Someone made this pattern.” (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:251-255`) and the protected closing's registry line (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:257`). The crest log and the closing's final “Someone had made the pattern” are separately mandatory protected text (`manuscript/chapter-58.md:229`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:267`) and are not new author composition.
+
+5. **Three protected gaps/overruns require source restoration.** The two markers remain in prose (`manuscript/chapter-54.md:323`; `manuscript/chapter-58.md:31`), and the authored continuation after “Twice. It'll hold twice…” displaces the source's actual end (`manuscript/chapter-55.md:29`; source `chapter-21.md:185`). Fixes 3–5 and 10–11 restore the source words and their joins.
+
+## Continuity that passes
+
+- **People, bodies, and standings:** Cael is nineteen (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:29-31`); Lira's left arm remains slung and holds nothing, while the taped ankle is never mended (`manuscript/chapter-58.md:17-21`; `manuscript/chapter-59.md:25-37`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:231-237`); Brom's shoulder opens, is mended a second time, then is bound rather than mended a third time (`manuscript/chapter-55.md:11-37,155`; `manuscript/chapter-56.md:35-61`; `manuscript/chapter-59.md:235-239`). These inherit the closed states at `manuscript/chapter-51.md:123-163` and `manuscript/chapter-52.md:5-75` without contradiction.
+- **Money and board:** the closed purse is 102 (`manuscript/chapter-52.md:357`); Karis pays six (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:7-11`), leaving ninety-six (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:11,31`). Pike has nine completed lines, no season number, and the five remain eleventh (`manuscript/chapter-59.md:167-219`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:31`). The Stair is “three hundred; taken; not paid” (`manuscript/chapter-59.md:175-179`), not a crew debt.
+- **Objects:** the Hall spends four of five bolts and leaves the last spanned in Oryn's bow with Lira (`manuscript/chapter-54.md:269-317`; `manuscript/chapter-55.md:121-129,155`; `manuscript/chapter-58.md:23-27`). Seln gives Karis the field ledger and does not reclaim it (`manuscript/chapter-59.md:99-123`). Karis has 11 Ring + 29 Stair + 12 Hall sheets = 52 (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:17-25`). The three boxes, sealed reserve, brown mule, grey jenny, map, two straightedges, Hesk's satchel, and Seln's shut case suffer no contradictory transfer in chapters 53–60 (`manuscript/chapter-53.md:63-65`; `manuscript/chapter-58.md:37-59`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:15-25,59-75,239-247`). Fix 18 makes every required component of the kit explicit on the ending page.
+- **Letters and accounts:** only the Hesk and Vell replies go west (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:75-87`); Ephram is deliberately deferred to the first thaw boat (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:85`). Oryn's letter is printed once (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:213-217`) and only paraphrased when read (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:221-227`). The ferryman's rope remains owed (`manuscript/chapter-59.md:145-157`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:91`).
+- **Knowledge:** six people know the mechanism; Teague is neither read nor asked and learns only observable outcomes (`manuscript/chapter-56.md:155-197`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:173-183`). Oryn still does not know Seln supplied Shadow, Karis's hypothesis remains unspoken/unentered, and no outsider learns that Cael's fragments work inside quiet ground (`manuscript/chapter-57.md:67-87`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:87-89,249-255`).
