+
+The withheld list passes after fixes: no name or entry for the fourth site and no Path test there (`manuscript/chapter-58.md:125-225`); no new theory of the still place (`manuscript/chapter-55.md:245-293`); Teague remains unread (`manuscript/chapter-56.md:155-197`); Karis's hypothesis stops at the pencil (`manuscript/chapter-57.md:79-87`); the instruments are true in Cael's hand (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:239-247`); and the body/equipment/money/ledger end states stand (`manuscript/chapter-58.md:17-27`; `manuscript/chapter-59.md:167-247`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:7-41`).
+
+## AUTHOR-REPORT owner flags
+
+1. **Line direction — KEEP.** Closed text puts the Fallow two days east of Thornwater (`manuscript/chapter-27.md:19-33,105-107,161-183`), the Stair west and south on the carter's distorted map, and the Hall south and east (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:79-81`; `manuscript/chapter-46.md:61-63`). The movement makes no true-ground compass claim for the alignment: it explicitly uses a map of counted days, a mile-wide strip, and ranging (`manuscript/chapter-53.md:19-33`; `manuscript/chapter-58.md:69-75`), then limits the finding to “as near as this skin can show” (`manuscript/chapter-57.md:65-77`). That is sufficient; the prose aligns paced centres on a fallible map without relocating roads.
+2. **“Twice…” — AMEND.** The protected unit ends with `and Brom said, "Arm," and she said, "No," and he didn't.` (source `chapter-21.md:185`). Fix 5 restores the whole unit and removes the conflicting authored six-day/third-mending speech (`manuscript/chapter-55.md:29`).
+3. **Two markers — AMEND.** Fixes 4 and 11 restore both exact source units (`manuscript/chapter-54.md:323`; `manuscript/chapter-58.md:31`).
+4. **Closing colon tags — KEEP.** They are source form, not plan shorthand (source `chapter-24.md:133-143`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:257-267`).
+5. **Oryn's letter once — KEEP.** Printed at `manuscript/chapter-60.md:217`, paraphrased at `:227`; no duplicate document.
+6. **“Three weeks” — AMEND THE JOIN, KEEP THE PROTECTED LINE.** The 104th-to-125th sum is exactly twenty-one days at the oxen ford (`manuscript/chapter-47.md:153,187`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:105-107,131-135`). “There” cannot honestly mean Thornwater under the edition's own sixteen-/seventeen-day route sums. Fix 10 establishes the oxen ford as its deictic referent; fix 11 supplies the source words with `after the thaw`. The BOOK_MAP §1 gloss “at Thornwater…three weeks late there” (`BOOK_MAP.md:37`) must be inherited by Book 8 as **three weeks at the oxen-ford account, Oryn physically at Thornwater**, not as a second arithmetic claim.
+7. **Old woman's knee — KEEP.** Oryn mends it at Millrace in closed Movement 7 (`manuscript/chapter-47.md:59-85`); the woman rests ten days, walks to Thornwater, and is checked there (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:151-179`). “The knee held” therefore has an observed referent (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:217`).
+8. **Deployment count — AMEND to twenty-seven.** See §1 and fixes 1–2, 6–8, 19. This also fits Book 8's entry statement that Anchor was “used both ways in Book 7” (`book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:68`) and supplies the exact final number that its reconciliation audit leaves open (`book-08-before-the-paths/state/B7-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:609`).
+9. **Ephram unanswered — KEEP.** The promise is on page and must pass to Book 8 (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:85`).
+10. **Clerk's packet west — KEEP.** It reports only that the crew kept what it was sent for (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:87-89`), not the mechanism.
+11. **Progression density — KEEP.** The system turns are present at the trial, Hall deployments, self-readings, inventory, and map (`manuscript/chapter-53.md:289-389`; `manuscript/chapter-54.md:179-293`; `manuscript/chapter-55.md:169-301`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:29-41,239-255`); no filler is warranted to chase a heuristic.
+12. **Chapter 57 POV ratio — KEEP.** Karis's window closes exactly on the pencil stopping and returns to Cael on day 121 (`manuscript/chapter-57.md:3-87,91`).
+13. **Unlisted additions — KEEP in part / AMEND in part.** Telling the other four shares the finding, not the reading mechanism, and is sound (`manuscript/chapter-57.md:191-209`). Oryn's arm check/bow refusal, her wordless gift of a fresh tape roll, Lira's ridge question, ferryman's rope, and Pike's first-snow custom are sound (`manuscript/chapter-58.md:17-27,85-89`; `manuscript/chapter-59.md:27,145-157,189-213`). Cael's cordon thought must be amended by fix 15 because this site's effect is unknown (`manuscript/chapter-58.md:161`).
+14. **Lira's edge-finding — AMEND strictly.** Sigil loss is a Path test and cannot coexist with “effect unknown”; fixes 13–16 keep her outside and use the visible iron boundary (`manuscript/chapter-58.md:149-185`).
+15. **Third “Twice.” — KEEP.** It is Oryn's answer to the unnamed healer, not a duplicate of the protected unit (`manuscript/chapter-56.md:43-49`).
+16. **Length — KEEP.** All eight chapters are complete and the movement closes on the mandated protected last word (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:267`).
+
+# 3. Calendar
+
