+2. **“Twice…” — AMEND.** The protected unit ends with `and Brom said, "Arm," and she said, "No," and he didn't.` (source `chapter-21.md:185`). Fix 5 restores the whole unit and removes the conflicting authored six-day/third-mending speech (`manuscript/chapter-55.md:29`).
+3. **Two markers — AMEND.** Fixes 4 and 11 restore both exact source units (`manuscript/chapter-54.md:323`; `manuscript/chapter-58.md:31`).
+4. **Closing colon tags — KEEP.** They are source form, not plan shorthand (source `chapter-24.md:133-143`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:257-267`).
+5. **Oryn's letter once — KEEP.** Printed at `manuscript/chapter-60.md:217`, paraphrased at `:227`; no duplicate document.
+6. **“Three weeks” — AMEND THE JOIN, KEEP THE PROTECTED LINE.** The 104th-to-125th sum is exactly twenty-one days at the oxen ford (`manuscript/chapter-47.md:153,187`; `manuscript/chapter-60.md:105-107,131-135`). “There” cannot honestly mean Thornwater under the edition's own sixteen-/seventeen-day route sums. Fix 10 establishes the oxen ford as its deictic referent; fix 11 supplies the source words with `after the thaw`. The BOOK_MAP §1 gloss “at Thornwater…three weeks late there” (`BOOK_MAP.md:37`) must be inherited by Book 8 as **three weeks at the oxen-ford account, Oryn physically at Thornwater**, not as a second arithmetic claim.
+7. **Old woman's knee — KEEP.** Oryn mends it at Millrace in closed Movement 7 (`manuscript/chapter-47.md:59-85`); the woman rests ten days, walks to Thornwater, and is checked there (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:151-179`). “The knee held” therefore has an observed referent (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:217`).
+8. **Deployment count — AMEND to twenty-seven.** See §1 and fixes 1–2, 6–7, and 19. This also fits Book 8's entry statement that Anchor was “used both ways in Book 7” (`book-08-before-the-paths/STATE_LEDGER.md:68`) and supplies the exact final number that its reconciliation audit leaves open (`book-08-before-the-paths/state/B7-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:609`).
+9. **Ephram unanswered — KEEP.** The promise is on page and must pass to Book 8 (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:85`).
+10. **Clerk's packet west — KEEP.** It reports only that the crew kept what it was sent for (`manuscript/chapter-60.md:87-89`), not the mechanism.
